{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition","id":1527154,"title":"My even-haded review of Werewolf: the Apocalypse Fifth Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-21T06:56:05-08:00","id":1527154,"title":"My even-haded review of Werewolf: the Apocalypse Fifth Edition","content":"<b>Warning - This review has a LONG intro that I couldn\u2019t cut down.</b><br /> <br /> WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE has always been about third or fourth in my favorite of the World of Darkness games. Which is not so much an insult or a question of its quality as the fact that I was an obsessive Vampire: The Masquerade and Mage: The Ascension player. Furthermore, I was brought into my fandom by Changeling: The Dreaming which was always the odd man out but a lot better game than most people ever did.<br /> <br /> The premise is that you are a, unsurprisingly, a werewolf and you are a warrior for Gaia the spirit of the Earth. Captain Planet jokes were being made even in the Nineties. The Earth is dying, and you have to stab or claw some folk to save her. Unfortunately, all Garou are good at is clawing or stabbing people, so they've unwittingly alienated or killed off all their fellow shifters as well as each other. One of the cooler elements of the premise is the Garou are a hammer that has been treating every problem as a nail for 20,000 years.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is a fantastic game and I'd argue that is probably the best written game after V:TM, even more so than Mage. However, like Mage, it suffered something of a problem with its own fandom. Without naming names, about 2000 or so, a developer told me the game had a white supremacy problem. A bunch of future Alt Right gamers were attracted to the game because of its themes despite the games' dogged (no pun intended) pro-indigenous rights and environmental themes. Clumsy writing, cultural appropriation, misuse of terms, and things like &quot;Pure Breed&quot; as a background meant the developers had way too many people taking the exact opposite of the message intended by the writers.<br /> <br /> If it feels like I'm digressing too much versus talking about the book, resolving a lot of those issues were major factors in the writing of Werewolf: The Apocalypse Revised and they've done even more overhauls to the Garou for 2023. Some of these changes have been ones that fans have been requesting for years, some of these make the game more like Werewolf: The Forsaken, and a few of these changes are just bad ideas.<br /> <br /> As usual, there's a bunch of behind-the-scenes drama that I won't get into, but I think is pretty much inevitable with competing artistic visions. Werewolf, like a proper World of Darkness game, says things and because of that someone is going to be offended. Sometimes rightly, in my opinion, so caveat emptor as the 5th Edition of the game is overall a mixed bag but not terrible from a lore or mechanics POV.<br /> <br /> Lore-wise the game takes the premise the Apocalypse is either happening or has happened with the Garou having lost the war. It takes the themes of the Garou screwing up saving Gaia to their natural conclusion and now most werewolves feel like the cause is hopeless. The Get of Fenris have become the Cult of Fenris and become fanatical zealots divorced from the rest of the Garou Nation. The fandom telephone game says the Cult have been taken over by Nazis and white supremacists but while you can read that into the text, they are only written as suffering the worst stereotypical behavior of old Garou being violent psychopaths who kill anything that they think is even vaguely Wyrm-y.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the mechanics have weaponized being an old school &quot;kill em all and let Gaia sort em out&quot; attitude of previous Werewolf editions and made it a condition like Harano (supernatural depression that I've always felt uncomfortable with as a neuroatypical person) called Hauglosk. The Get falling to evil is a very questionable thing as they were one of the more popular tribes and it seems strange to have them go full fanatic while the Red Talons remain part of the Garou Nation. Out of game, it seems this condition basically exists to clarify the Garou\u2019s history of violence to solve all their problems was idiotic. Which I thought was clear from 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> Other changes include getting rid of Crinosborn (my term for Garou-Garou children versus the one they used to use) and getting rid of the genetic component of the race. Like the Force, certain families have stronger chances of being Garou but it's not a 100% genetically inherited trait. Which admittedly does tone down the issues of Kinfolk from previous editions. Oddly, I'd say that is the much bigger retcon than anything related to the Get. Mind you, the game wants to have its cake and eat it too as some Garou clearly believe it\u2019s still genetic but it's now clear that they're flat out wrong. Still, I wanted to know about how this affected Garou-Garou marriages, their relationships with mortal families, and more. Maybe next book.<br /> <br /> The tribes have been divorced of their historical cultural origins, which is a more questionable action as well despite understanding the logic thereof. The Fianna have become the Hart Wardens while the indigenous tribes have become Galestalkers and Ghost Council. I won't even use their original names because they turned out to have been highly insulting so, good call. Ditto my favorite tribe of Samuel Haight's tribe (which, again, was a no-no in its name). They're now called the Stolen Moons. Overall, I understand the decision-making process here and mostly think it was a good idea to re-examine the handling of indigenous culture among Garou.<br /> <br /> Without going into another digression, basically indigenous rights were always a major background theme of Werewolf and clumsily handled. If you wonder how clumsily handled, a pair of examples is the fact there used to be tribes called the Croatoan (descended from South Carolina Native Americans) and Bunyip (Aboriginal Werewolves) before they went extinct. The problem being the Croatoan are a real-life ethnic group that some people still claim ancestry of today and, well, I\u2019ve talked to Australian gamers of said descent who would like to point out their ethnic group is still around so why can\u2019t they be werewolves?<br /> <br /> Thus, these groups have been reduced to septs or \u201cmicro-tribes\u201d with a page lamenting European colonization\u2019s effects before moving on. Is it a good thing or a bad thing to reduce the role of native peoples in Werewolf when so much of the original game was about Western civilization encroaching on traditional peoples? I dunno. The original game took a heavy pro-First Peoples stance in a clumsy and ham-fisted way primarily written by well-meaning white dudes. I support the message even though it was badly framed. Strictly speaking, though, now you can just use the existing Garou tribes anywhere on Earth and give them local variants.<br /> <br /> After having spent a thousand words discussing the politics of a Nineties Gothic Punk game moved into the 2020s, how is the actual game? Well, it's fine. It's a bit less focused. Adding an existentialist element to the setting about the fact the war against the Wyrm is probably pointless opens more storytelling opportunities. Climate change activists may think now is the most important time to be fighting Pentex but the urgency is gone if you want to run a sept just about looking after your old neighborhood. The Garou aren\u2019t going to save the world on their own so they might as well save their whatever we\u2019re calling kinfolk now.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the game is fine and will function for what the player wants it to as well as the Storytellers. I don't have any objection to the changes that feel comparatively tame versus Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition's. Gifts are tied to Willpower and Renown instead of Gnosis (which no longer exists). The addition of Loresheets is also welcome as I've always found those to be exceptionally useful. Speaking of similarities, the book also indicates the Second Inquisition knows about Garou and is hunting them as well. Just not in the numbers or with the same success as vampires (which makes sense given the Delerium).<br /> <br /> So, what\u2019s my take? Eh, my take on Fifth Edition is that it is a deeply uneven revision. It\u2019s got some good ideas and some bad ideas. I feel like the depth of the changes are somewhat exaggerated, though, and people have read into things that aren\u2019t there. I disagree with some of the choices while am generally able to follow the logic of most decisions. Was vilifying the Get of Fenris a good idea? No. They should have made a rival sect of the Garou Nation of multiple tribes and kept the Viking werewolves. Was changing a bunch of the terminology and getting rid of the whole Crinosborn thing a good idea? I believe so, yeah. Let Garou mate with Garou so sayeth Albretch! Was getting rid of the entirety of the complicated relationship between Garou and kinfolk a good idea? No, but I'm not sure they did. They just sort of gloss over it. The de-emphasizing of Garou relationships to local people? That is a very complicated subject and they could have done much better there. Overall, I am going to be the one most shocked by saying my review is mostly positive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T08:14:33-08:00","id":1527161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition#post1527154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding an existentialist element to the setting about the fact the war against the Wyrm is probably pointless opens more storytelling opportunities. Climate change activists may think now is the most important time to be fighting Pentex but the urgency is gone if you want to run a sept just about looking after your old neighborhood. The Garou aren\u2019t going to save the world on their own so they might as well save their whatever we\u2019re calling kinfolk now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel this is going to be forever a taste thing, but I have to disagree with this.<br /> <br /> If you want to have a game involving and discussing climate change, pollution and such, you shouldn't then present the default mentality towards it as 'we can't do anything about it.' If the tagline remains &quot;When Will You Rage?&quot;, you should keep this sense of hope and struggle as the main solution. We in IRL are already struggling with doomerism, let's not make it the default stance of the game about fighting back.<br /> <br /> This is why I would have preferred they had done something not related to all the above, if they did not want to get in the weeds about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T08:18:20-08:00","id":1527162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition#post1527154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Warning - This review has a LONG intro that I couldn\u2019t cut down.</b><br /> <br /> WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE has always been about third or fourth in my favorite of the World of Darkness games. Which is not so much an insult or a question of its quality as the fact that I was an obsessive Vampire: The Masquerade and Mage: The Ascension player. Furthermore, I was brought into my fandom by Changeling: The Dreaming which was always the odd man out but a lot better game than most people ever did.<br /> <br /> The premise is that you are a, unsurprisingly, a werewolf and you are a warrior for Gaia the spirit of the Earth. Captain Planet jokes were being made even in the Nineties. The Earth is dying</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It is being killed, and the people responsible etc. etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and you have to stab or claw some folk to save her. Unfortunately, all Garou are good at is clawing or stabbing people, so they've unwittingly alienated or killed off all their fellow shifters as well as each other. One of the cooler elements of the premise is the Garou are a hammer that has been treating every problem as a nail for 20,000 years.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is a fantastic game and I'd argue that is probably the best written game after V:TM, even more so than Mage. However, like Mage, it suffered something of a problem with its own fandom. Without naming names, about 2000 or so, a developer told me the game had a white supremacy problem. A bunch of future Alt Right gamers were attracted to the game because of its themes despite the games' dogged (no pun intended) pro-indigenous rights and environmental themes. Clumsy writing, cultural appropriation, misuse of terms, and things like &quot;Pure Breed&quot; as a background meant the developers had way too many people taking the exact opposite of the message intended by the writers. </div> </div> </div>A missed opportunity when W20 came out. Just like how Past Life was renamed to Ancestors, I wish that PB had been renamed to Tribe Legacy (it's not transferable between tribes; if you have it for one but join another, you don't get it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it feels like I'm digressing too much versus talking about the book, resolving a lot of those issues were major factors in the writing of Werewolf: The Apocalypse Revised and they've done even more overhauls to the Garou for 2023. Some of these changes have been ones that fans have been requesting for years, some of these make the game more like Werewolf: The Forsaken, and a few of these changes are just bad ideas.<br /> <br /> As usual, there's a bunch of behind-the-scenes drama that I won't get into, but I think is pretty much inevitable with competing artistic visions. Werewolf, like a proper World of Darkness game, says things and because of that someone is going to be offended. Sometimes rightly, in my opinion, so caveat emptor as the 5th Edition of the game is overall a mixed bag but not terrible from a lore or mechanics POV.<br /> <br /> Lore-wise the game takes the premise the Apocalypse is either happening or has happened with the Garou having lost the war. It takes the themes of the Garou screwing up saving Gaia to their natural conclusion and now most werewolves feel like the cause is hopeless. The Get of Fenris have become the Cult of Fenris and become fanatical zealots divorced from the rest of the Garou Nation. The fandom telephone game says the Cult have been taken over by Nazis and white supremacists but while you can read that into the text, they are only written as suffering the worst stereotypical behavior of old Garou being violent psychopaths who kill anything that they think is even vaguely Wyrm-y.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the mechanics have weaponized being an old school &quot;kill em all and let Gaia sort em out&quot; attitude of previous Werewolf editions and made it a condition like Harano (supernatural depression that I've always felt uncomfortable with as a neuroatypical person) called Hauglosk. The Get falling to evil is a very questionable thing as they were one of the more popular tribes and it seems strange to have them go full fanatic while the Red Talons remain part of the Garou Nation. Out of game, it seems this condition basically exists to clarify the Garou\u2019s history of violence to solve all their problems was idiotic. Which I thought was clear from 1st Edition. </div> </div> </div>Hauglosk was tagged as a way to introduce eco-fascism into the game. The CoF are all in Hauglosk. It logically follows that Karim got what he wanted in making the Fenrir all Swords of Heimdall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other changes include getting rid of Crinosborn (my term for Garou-Garou children versus the one they used to use) and getting rid of the genetic component of the race. Like the Force, certain families have stronger chances of being Garou but it's not a 100% genetically inherited trait. Which admittedly does tone down the issues of Kinfolk from previous editions. Oddly, I'd say that is the much bigger retcon than anything related to the Get. Mind you, the game wants to have its cake and eat it too as some Garou clearly believe it\u2019s still genetic but it's now clear that they're flat out wrong. Still, I wanted to know about how this affected Garou-Garou marriages, their relationships with mortal families, and more. Maybe next book. </div> </div> </div>Not actually genetic; if you try to clone a Garou, per the Revised Storyteller's Handbook, you get a Kinfolk human or wolf, or a dead Crinos-born fetus (bearing Crinos-born requires a living being with Rage, per the text). Ultimately, it was always down to Gaia deciding, but because that's a complicated matter that no one's ever going to untangle and you can't really go and speak to Gaia proper (only an avatar of her avatar, or possibly a being even further from the source than that), the Garou and Fera experience it as a statistical generality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The tribes have been divorced of their historical cultural origins, which is a more questionable action as well despite understanding the logic thereof. The Fianna have become the Hart Wardens while the indigenous tribes have become Galestalkers and Ghost Council. I won't even use their original names because they turned out to have been highly insulting so, good call. Ditto my favorite tribe of Samuel Haight's tribe (which, again, was a no-no in its name). They're now called the Stolen Moons. Overall, I understand the decision-making process here and mostly think it was a good idea to re-examine the handling of indigenous culture among Garou.<br /> <br /> Without going into another digression, basically indigenous rights were always a major background theme of Werewolf and clumsily handled. If you wonder how clumsily handled, a pair of examples is the fact there used to be tribes called the Croatoan (descended from South Carolina Native Americans) and Bunyip (Aboriginal Werewolves) before they went extinct. The problem being the Croatoan are a real-life ethnic group that some people still claim ancestry of today and, well, I\u2019ve talked to Australian gamers of said descent who would like to point out their ethnic group is still around so why can\u2019t they be werewolves? </div> </div> </div>Turtle's tribe was actually all throughout the northern part of the continent down to Mesoamerica. They actually lived with the peoples who made most of the cities that got emptied out by disease from the Europeans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thus, these groups have been reduced to septs or \u201cmicro-tribes\u201d with a page lamenting European colonization\u2019s effects before moving on. Is it a good thing or a bad thing to reduce the role of native peoples in Werewolf when so much of the original game was about Western civilization encroaching on traditional peoples? I dunno. The original game took a heavy pro-First Peoples stance in a clumsy and ham-fisted way primarily written by well-meaning white dudes. </div> </div> </div>Now it's all white dudes all the time! All the way from Europe, with no care or regard for this at all!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I support the message even though it was badly framed. Strictly speaking, though, now you can just use the existing Garou tribes anywhere on Earth and give them local variants. </div> </div> </div>That's not new to this edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After having spent a thousand words discussing the politics of a Nineties Gothic Punk game moved into the 2020s, how is the actual game? Well, it's fine. It's a bit less focused. Adding an existentialist element to the setting about the fact the war against the Wyrm is probably pointless opens more storytelling opportunities. Climate change activists may think now is the most important time to be fighting Pentex but the urgency is gone if you want to run a sept just about looking after your old neighborhood. The Garou aren\u2019t going to save the world on their own so they might as well save their whatever we\u2019re calling kinfolk now. </div> </div> </div>Kinfolk don't exist in this edition. Like, at all. The term Kin is used where past editions would have used Lost Cub or the like, i.e. a Garou who hasn't changed yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mechanically, the game is fine and will function for what the player wants it to as well as the Storytellers. I don't have any objection to the changes that feel comparatively tame versus Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition's. Gifts are tied to Willpower and Renown instead of Gnosis (which no longer exists). The addition of Loresheets is also welcome as I've always found those to be exceptionally useful. Speaking of similarities, the book also indicates the Second Inquisition knows about Garou and is hunting them as well. Just not in the numbers or with the same success as vampires (which makes sense given the Delerium). </div> </div> </div>With the typical caveat that if what you want is personal horror done in a certain way, you'll have no complaints. However, this hasn't ever really been the focus of W:tA, nor have any of the mechanical tidbits that focus it in W5 ever really been nearly as central as presented. They were not Hunger; they were only a slight shade more frequent than fucking Golconda.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, what\u2019s my take? Eh, my take on Fifth Edition is that it is a deeply uneven revision. It\u2019s got some good ideas and some bad ideas. I feel like the depth of the changes are somewhat exaggerated, though, and people have read into things that aren\u2019t there. I disagree with some of the choices while am generally able to follow the logic of most decisions. Was vilifying the Get of Fenris a good idea? No. They should have made a rival sect of the Garou Nation of multiple tribes and kept the Viking werewolves. Was changing a bunch of the terminology and getting rid of the whole Crinosborn thing a good idea? I believe so, yeah. Let Garou mate with Garou so sayeth Albretch! Was getting rid of the entirety of the complicated relationship between Garou and kinfolk a good idea? No, but I'm not sure they did. They just sort of gloss over it. The de-emphasizing of Garou relationships to local people? That is a very complicated subject and they could have done much better there. Overall, I am going to be the one most shocked by saying my review is mostly positive. </div> </div> </div>Figures that a Vampire main would say that. (^VVVVVV^)<br /> <br /> (PS The GoF have not been centered around being vikings for way longer than they were.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T09:14:41-08:00","id":1527165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fandom telephone game says the Cult have been taken over by Nazis and white supremacists but while you can read that into the text, they are only written as suffering the worst stereotypical behavior of old Garou being violent psychopaths who kill anything that they think is even vaguely Wyrm-y. </div> </div> </div>I don't know why people keep getting this wrong. The book is pretty clear about this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From pg 321:<br /> <br /> <b>Fascism</b><br /> <br /> Werewolf is not a fascist friendly game. Because it\u2019s a horror game about contemporary issues, it can be a game where fascism as a theme or fascists as characters show<br /> up. After all, they\u2019re an unfortunate part of the real world we all inhabit.<br /> <br /> In the simplest terms, you can use <b>Nazis of whatever stripe seems most appropriate</b> for your setting as enemies. After all, who doesn\u2019t want to go full Wolfenstein every now and then? In Werewolf, you can confront the problems of the world and rip their face off. Nazis are certainly a problem!<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Note that in Werewolf, themes of fascism may be present in the social realm of the players\u2019 characters. <b>A friend goes over to the Cult of Fenris, seduced by their<br /> message of simpleminded morality.</b> <b>A player may decide to explore themes of ecofascism in their own character by skirting close to hauglosk</b>. These situations <b>create opportunities to grapple with fascism with more nuance than as simple enemies</b>. </div> </div> </div> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> I mean, come on... It's pretty obvious that the &quot;Get of Fenris=Nazis&quot;-idea is very much alive in the W5 corebook. Now the idea of advising players that playing fascist PCs is a valid way to play W5 is a whole other can of worms I wouldn't normally expect to see in a section on &quot;considerate play&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a bit less focused. Adding an existentialist element to the setting about the fact the war against the Wyrm is probably pointless opens more storytelling opportunities. Climate change activists may think now is the most important time to be fighting Pentex but the urgency is gone if you want to run a sept just about looking after your old neighborhood. The Garou aren\u2019t going to save the world on their own so they might as well save their whatever we\u2019re calling kinfolk now. </div> </div> </div>That is a change in direction that I would simply consider bad worldbuilding. Talk about missing the forest for the trees... I get it, they wanted their &quot;street-level-only&quot; but come on, the game is called &quot;Werewolf: The <i>Apocalypse</i>&quot;. The moment you get to the point of saying &quot;The Apocalypse? Nah, don't worry about it... that's old news. It's already happening, nothing you can do about it.&quot;, the developers have just lost the plot. It's like making it a central element for the fifth edition of Mage the Ascension that due to the bad state of the world, Ascension is now actually impossible, thereby rendering the Ascension-War pointless. At that point, the developers would've been better off just making a new game altogether. If the core premise is rejected to this degree, it's questionable whether there's even a point in continuing that creative exercise.<br /> <br /> Now I would grant that an interesting alternative would've been to delve into the idea of what it's like living through the Apocalypse - but W5 isn't nearly that interesting. As you mentioned, it's more about taking focus away by shrinking the horizon the corebook is willing to explore.<br /> <br /> _________________________________________________<br /> <br /> On the bright side, I gotta say one thing: W5 is way better than H5. So in that comparison, W5 comes off better. And if you think about how troubled the development of this book has been and how many changes and missteps occured... Switching creative teams from Hunters Entertainment to the in-house WOD-team, Justin Achilli leaving before the end of development, the issue with the art, last-minute changes to Tribe-names... It feels like a bit of a miracle the book was released this year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T09:33:55-08:00","id":1527166,"title":"","content":"While I do appreciate you sharing your opinions on this, it does feel like quite an unfair jab at everyone else that yours is more &quot;even-headed&quot;. You might not agree or see the the differences some people do, but your opinion is as valid as theirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T10:13:56-08:00","id":1527172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527166#post1527166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do appreciate you sharing your opinions on this, it does feel like quite an unfair jab at everyone else that yours is more &quot;even-headed&quot;. You might not agree or see the the differences some people do, but your opinion is as valid as theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's meant to be a description of the review itself, not other people's review.<br /> <br /> I like some things, I dislike other things.<br /> <br /> I am not filled with gushing praise for the work nor am I am filled with incredible hatred. I'm happy to hear another way to describe my review if you want me to ask the mods to rename it. I have no interest in running down other posters or their work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T10:41:59-08:00","id":1527174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527161#post1527161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel this is going to be forever a taste thing, but I have to disagree with this.<br /> <br /> If you want to have a game involving and discussing climate change, pollution and such, you shouldn't then present the default mentality towards it as 'we can't do anything about it.' If the tagline remains &quot;When Will You Rage?&quot;, you should keep this sense of hope and struggle as the main solution. We in IRL are already struggling with doomerism, let's not make it the default stance of the game about fighting back.<br /> <br /> This is why I would have preferred they had done something not related to all the above, if they did not want to get in the weeds about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I suspect it is a matter of taste but I'd also point out that doomerism is also accompanied by the element of the fact that it was corporations like Pentex in the Real World (I am now of the mind that anything Pentex does is less weird or vile or cult driven than the ideologies of RL capitalism) created the personal responsibility form of environmentalism when it was always going to be large scale systemic change as well as government action necessary. That has little to do with the idea of coping with helplessness on a personal level or the depression therein but I think that's worthwhile in an RPG.<br /> <br /> It definitely may not be the attitude you want at your table, though, and I fully understand that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527162#post1527162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. It is being killed, and the people responsible etc. etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>People being killed are, in fact, dying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527162#post1527162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A missed opportunity when W20 came out. Just like how Past Life was renamed to Ancestors, I wish that PB had been renamed to Tribe Legacy (it's not transferable between tribes; if you have it for one but join another, you don't get it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I never felt Pure Breed was that smart of an idea even way back when and felt dissonant with the line since the Garou already had Renown as a system. After all, why would any werewolf care about how much you look like a stereotypical member of the tribe? There were defections between tribes even then.<br /> <br /> [quote=Saur Ops Specialist;n1527162]Hauglosk was tagged as a way to introduce eco-fascism into the game. The CoF are all in Hauglosk. It logically follows that Karim got what he wanted in making the Fenrir all Swords of Heimdall.<br /> <br /> Tagged that way or not, it pretty much is just the exact same attitude the worst stereotypes of the Garou were dealing with in-universe anyway. I was a 1st to Revised Man and never got into W20 but there was always the &quot;New Impergium&quot;, &quot;the Garou aren't violent enough&quot;, or other Thanos solution for human evils types as everyone ignored the Children of Gaia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527162#post1527162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not actually genetic; if you try to clone a Garou, per the Revised Storyteller's Handbook, you get a Kinfolk human or wolf, or a dead Crinos-born fetus (bearing Crinos-born requires a living being with Rage, per the text). Ultimately, it was always down to Gaia deciding, but because that's a complicated matter that no one's ever going to untangle and you can't really go and speak to Gaia proper (only an avatar of her avatar, or possibly a being even further from the source than that), the Garou and Fera experience it as a statistical generality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad they spelled it out is all I'm saying.<br /> <br /> [quote=Saur Ops Specialist;n1527162]Turtle's tribe was actually all throughout the northern part of the continent down to Mesoamerica. They actually lived with the peoples who made most of the cities that got emptied out by disease from the Europeans.<br /> <br /> Doesn't that make it worse? It is just making them more and &quot;the people slaughtered by Europeans&quot; and, again, those people's descendants are almost all still around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527162#post1527162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now it's all white dudes all the time! All the way from Europe, with no care or regard for this at all!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the Rage across Russia acknowledgement. They had the entirety of the tribes there and it worked pretty well way back when.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527162#post1527162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinfolk don't exist in this edition. Like, at all. The term Kin is used where past editions would have used Lost Cub or the like, i.e. a Garou who hasn't changed yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the book is direly lacking in contact of what, if any, role that human family members play in the setting and I hope we'll get an update on them soon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527162#post1527162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the typical caveat that if what you want is personal horror done in a certain way, you'll have no complaints. However, this hasn't ever really been the focus of W:tA, nor have any of the mechanical tidbits that focus it in W5 ever really been nearly as central as presented. They were not Hunger; they were only a slight shade more frequent than fucking Golconda.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really feel like there's much focus on personal horror in this installment of the game. The Garou are still rage monsters meant to kill things. There's more a melancholy sense of loss and failure but it's mostly just taken the piss out of the idea that killing things was ever going to fix the planet. The idea that the Garou's Rage utterly fucked up their entire purpose has been there since 1st Edition with the Imperium, War of Rage, and the idea behind Evan Heals the Past that wouldn't be a character we never talked about if they'd just done the senisble thing and made the kid a Child of Gaia and not a white boy who attended his first college courses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527162#post1527162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Figures that a Vampire main would say that. (^VVVVVV^)</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, it took the Sabbat and Second Inquisition books to finally turn me off V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527162#post1527162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(PS The GoF have not been centered around being vikings for way longer than they were.)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel like my issues with this Edition can be summarized by pointing out that if they wanted to remove the Tribes from their cultural origins then maybe one of them shouldn't be named after a giant wolf of Norse mythology.<br /> <br /> Make THEM the Winter's Teeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T11:50:23-08:00","id":1527178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527174#post1527174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, I suspect it is a matter of taste but I'd also point out that doomerism is also accompanied by the element of the fact that it was corporations like Pentex in the Real World (I am now of the mind that anything Pentex does is less weird or vile or cult driven than the ideologies of RL capitalism) created the personal responsibility form of environmentalism when it was always going to be large scale systemic change as well as government action necessary. That has little to do with the idea of coping with helplessness on a personal level or the depression therein but I think that's worthwhile in an RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I have with it isn't really addressing that need for systematic change and the feeling of doom. It is that it is all there truly is, a sense of 'well, we fucked up.' That is great for a few sessions, but at some point, there has to be a conclusion to the conflict, and W5 seems unwilling to progress that far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527174#post1527174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like my issues with this Edition can be summarized by pointing out that if they wanted to remove the Tribes from their cultural origins then maybe one of them shouldn't be named after a giant wolf of Norse mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dislike ad hominem, but I feel leaving the Nordic elements in CoF was intentional due to the Brand Manager's obsession with vilifying the tribe. From all the evidence J.F.Sambrano has given (which I know is only one side of the story), Muammar has an issue with the Fenrir <i>because</i> they are the Nordic tribe. So keeping the elements there is, in effect, saying that holding onto cultural ties is drawing you to extremism. And there are groups in Sweden IRL who very much are misusing their viking ancestors as justification for racism.<br /> <br /> This is just my own theory, of course. But without the baggage of IRL issues, I can't really see Red Talons being ignored as the best case for the 'bad tribe.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T11:53:39-08:00","id":1527179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527178#post1527178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike ad hominem, but I feel leaving the Nordic elements in CoF was intentional due to the Brand Manager's obsession with vilifying the tribe. From all the evidence J.F.Sambrano has given (which I know is only one side of the story), Muammar has an issue with the Fenrir <i>because</i> they are the Nordic tribe. So keeping the elements there is, in effect, saying that holding onto cultural ties is drawing you to extremism. And there are groups in Sweden IRL who very much are misusing their viking ancestors as justification for racism.<br /> <br /> This is just my own theory, of course. But without the baggage of IRL issues, I can't really see Red Talons being ignored as the best case for the 'bad tribe.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Sambrano deserves all the credit for giving us an inside look into the making of the sausage and his efforts to promote an indiginous perspective. He has been clear that his view on the handling of the Get was as a fan, though, not as an issue personal to his heart like Older Brother and Younger Brother.<br /> <br /> Which is a long way of going about to say that Karim Muammar as a Swiss Punk may have OPINIONS on Nordic appropriation by the Alt Right that I don't necessarily feel like it's my place to begrudge him.<br /> <br /> Even so, what I brought up earlier is the Get of Fenris aren't literally Nazis or racists. Their depiction in the book is that their leadership has become fanatical and bloodthirsty in a very traditionally Garou-esque way and are doubling down on the violence as a solution to the Apocalypse. Which is a lot more nuanced take than some people are depicting it.<br /> <br /> It's not &quot;The Swords of Heimdall are back and have taken over!&quot; so much as, &quot;The Get plan to kill every capitalist and literer they can lay their hands on. Also, kill any Garou who disagrees with this policy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-21-2023, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T12:26:11-08:00","id":1527181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527172#post1527172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm happy to hear another way to describe my review if you want me to ask the mods to rename it. I have no interest in running down other posters or their work.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mixed&quot; is pretty much the default review terminology for a reaction that doesn't lean to favorable or unfavorable for whatever reasons.<br /> <br /> &quot;Even-handed&quot; implies a level of process &quot;fairness.&quot; And even-handed review can still be scathing or effusive if the general feeling is that the reviewer made their case as fairly as possible. Trying to avoid fair, but harsh/glowing criticism is what drives so much media (from reviews to the news) into both-sides style issues where the appearance of impartiality overrides actually stating a definitive conclusion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527179#post1527179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a long way of going about to say that Karim Muammar as a Swiss Punk may have OPINIONS on Nordic appropriation by the Alt Right that I don't necessarily feel like it's my place to begrudge him.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, exactly, has Karim done to earn the title &quot;punk&quot; exactly?<br /> <br /> And sure, he has opinions, but his opinions got in the way of making the game better. His leaked comments are how we know the intent was for the Cult of Fenris to be the Swords of Heimdall triumphant. That's what he wanted, and he had to be talked down from that position (since it makes no sense with the non-cultural Garou of W5 to have a group of literal Nazis taking over a Tribe as one of the antagonists).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is a lot more nuanced take than some people are depicting it. </div> </div> </div>Based on... what? What passages in the text actually support this?<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris has fallen to Hauglosk. Hauglosk is a fantasy mental illness that makes you become a fascist if you try too hard to fix the broken world (it's been cited above).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not &quot;The Swords of Heimdall are back and have taken over!&quot; so much as, &quot;The Get plan to kill every capitalist and literer they can lay their hands on. Also, kill any Garou who disagrees with this policy.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Where is the Cult of Fenris ever shown to actually be this? Also, even if this were the case, it only proves how bad the lore is, because according to the books, capitalists are the only large scale organizing force that can have positive change in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T12:44:56-08:00","id":1527186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527181#post1527181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Mixed&quot; is pretty much the default review terminology for a reaction that doesn't lean to favorable or unfavorable for whatever reasons.<br /> <br /> &quot;Even-handed&quot; implies a level of process &quot;fairness.&quot; And even-handed review can still be scathing or effusive if the general feeling is that the reviewer made their case as fairly as possible. Trying to avoid fair, but harsh/glowing criticism is what drives so much media (from reviews to the news) into both-sides style issues where the appearance of impartiality overrides actually stating a definitive conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>So noted and if the moderators can change the title to &quot;My mixed review of Werewolf: Fifth Edition&quot; then I'd be okay with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What, exactly, has Karim done to earn the title &quot;punk&quot; exactly? </div> </div> </div>Punk is not a title to be earned but simply an ethos. Not that any punk agrees with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And sure, he has opinions, but his opinions got in the way of making the game better. His leaked comments are how we know the intent was for the Cult of Fenris to be the Swords of Heimdall triumphant. That's what he wanted, and he had to be talked down from that position (since it makes no sense with the non-cultural Garou of W5 to have a group of literal Nazis taking over a Tribe as one of the antagonists). </div> </div> </div>The final results are the Get of Fernis not being racially motivated so there's definitely that. I have nothing against Nazi punching in my game and my characters have slaughtered many a Hydra, Technocracy (who are absolutely irredeemable bastards in my modern games), and other Alt Right stand in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Based on... what? What passages in the text actually support this? </div> </div> </div><i>At a great meeting of the tribes, the Cult of Fenris<br /> called for one final, glorious charge into the Wyrm\u2019s maw<br /> to avert the Apocalypse, but the assembled Garou of<br /> other tribes called out their rally as suicide, whereupon<br /> most of the Cult of Fenris camp decided that all Garou<br /> had fallen, and only the Cult\u2019s pure vision could serve<br /> Gaia. After a torturously long and bloody duel among<br /> champions of the tribes at the grand moot, renowned<br /> Garou solemnly declared a deadlock, and the Cult of<br /> Fenris abandoned the tribes to their fates, pledging their<br /> enmity and exiting the gathering. </i><br /> <br /> <i>The tribe\u2019s outlook is one of nonfalsifiable orthodoxy<br /> \u2014 impurity is everywhere and everything is the Wyrm\u2019s<br /> fault, and to disagree with this perspective is proof of<br /> one\u2019s own collusion with the Wyrm. From the outside,<br /> many Garou wonder if those among the Cult of Fenris<br /> have themselves been misled into pluralistic hauglosk by<br /> pernicious leaders, tricked into serving the Wyrm\u2019s ends<br /> by blindly raging against it in everything they see. Were<br /> such betrayal the case, theurges argue, the Cult would<br /> not even truly be following Wolf anymore, but some<br /> aspect of the Wyrm \u2014 unless Wolf himself has led what<br /> remains of his tribe into Wyrm-thrall\u2026. Unthinkable.</i> <b>Page 259</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThe take on the Cult of Fenris in the book is that they're a bunch of super-Garou theological fanatics that are trying to go after the Wyrm with reckless abandon. That's not, &quot;We believe only white people should be Cult of Fenris and all Garou should be Cult of Fenris.&quot; They're basically just following the typical Garou theology to its fundamentalist reactionary conclusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Cult of Fenris has fallen to Hauglosk. Hauglosk is a fantasy mental illness that makes you become a fascist if you try too hard to fix the broken world (it's been cited above). </div> </div> </div>Specifically, it is a faux mental illness to represent fascism that violence is the solution to all your problems and if something doesn't work you just aren't trying to do it hard enough. Also, the Garou believe the Get ELDERS have fallen to hauglosk not the Cult of Fenris as a whole.<br /> <br /> Note that you only get Hauglosk points when you violate a Chronicle tenet so literally you have to be a bastard against what the Chronicle is about to get any (unless you use it like the Dark Side of the Force for extra Willpower points).<br /> <br /> <i>Every time a werewolf violates a chronicle Tenet (see<br /> p. 199) they must make a Hauglosk test, with a dice pool<br /> equal to the amount of filled boxes of both the harano<br /> and hauglosk trackers. (This test is made at a minimum<br /> of one die; do not use Rage dice for this test.) The<br /> Difficulty is usually 1, but the Storyteller can decide<br /> that severe violations or transgressions warrant a higher<br /> Difficulty. Failing the test results in a box being filled on<br /> the hauglosk tracker, from left to right. If the tracker ever<br /> becomes filled, the werewolf has succumbed to hauglosk,<br /> becoming an unredeemable fanatic and a Storyteller<br /> character.\u200b </i><b>Page 141</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where is the Cult of Fenris ever shown to actually be this? Also, even if this were the case, it only proves how bad the lore is, because according to the books, capitalists are the only large scale organizing force that can have positive change in the WoD. </div> </div> </div><i>The specific manifestations of hauglosk can take<br /> many forms. It\u2019s common for those who are afflicted to<br /> justify ever greater human casualties, ignore their own<br /> mistakes, and argue that everyone with even the mildest<br /> and most subjective whiff of corruption deserves to die.<br /> (In fact, such absolute terms are indicators, themselves<br /> \u2014 \u201ccorruption\u201d of that which is pure, \u201cdegenerate\u201d<br /> behavior or conditions, \u201csympathy\u201d for those who don\u2019t<br /> deserve it\u2026.) They often declare Garou who don\u2019t agree<br /> with them to be blood enemies, subject to even greater<br /> hatred than what a rampant Apocalypse has wrought<br /> upon the world.\u200b</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T12:53:31-08:00","id":1527188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527174#post1527174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> People being killed are, in fact, dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not of illness, or because winter is setting in and they've reached their limit, or as a sacrifice. Being killed means that someone is actively giving them the poison, leaving them out in the cold, stabbing the knife into their heart, etc. There's an agency there that &quot;dying&quot; is more neutral about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh, I never felt Pure Breed was that smart of an idea even way back when and felt dissonant with the line since the Garou already had Renown as a system. After all, why would any werewolf care about how much you look like a stereotypical member of the tribe? There were defections between tribes even then. </div> </div> </div>Because it's a Heroic Lineage and Garou are tied to their ancestors rather closely. You know, in editions of Werewolf that mean something and have the Ancestors background to explain, partially, why things got fucked up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tagged that way or not, it pretty much is just the exact same attitude the worst stereotypes of the Garou were dealing with in-universe anyway. I was a 1st to Revised Man and never got into W20 but there was always the &quot;New Impergium&quot;, &quot;the Garou aren't violent enough&quot;, or other Thanos solution for human evils types as everyone ignored the Children of Gaia. </div> </div> </div>No one who was agitating for a &quot;New Impergium&quot; was being realistic in any way, shape, or form. The Revised Tribebooks came down on it, the previous tribebooks had the Red Talons laugh bitterly at the idea and had them essentially say, &quot;Don't you see? It's already here; it is how humans treat wolves.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm glad they spelled it out is all I'm saying. </div> </div> </div>What, like in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook? Which came out around two decades ago?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doesn't that make it worse? It is just making them more and &quot;the people slaughtered by Europeans&quot; and, again, those people's descendants are almost all still around. </div> </div> </div>Yes. It wasn't a defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think this is the Rage across Russia acknowledgement. They had the entirety of the tribes there and it worked pretty well way back when. </div> </div> </div>RAR still had problems with the various tribes consisting of ethnic enclaves and expatriates. Furies are described as having very strong Greek ties instead of being Russian, the Get are from North Europe instead of being Russian, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, the book is direly lacking in contact of what, if any, role that human family members play in the setting and I hope we'll get an update on them soon. </div> </div> </div>I think you'd be only slightly less likely to see rules for Gnosis back in the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't really feel like there's much focus on personal horror in this installment of the game. </div> </div> </div>I guess if you're swimming in it more frequently it might not seem like much, but there's a distinct lack of battle scars and, as noted, a double-barreled degeneration mechanic even harsher than what's in Vampire, since there's practically no going back. You can sweep the points around, but eventually you'll pile it too high.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou are still rage monsters meant to kill things. There's more a melancholy sense of loss and failure but it's mostly just taken the piss out of the idea that killing things was ever going to fix the planet. The idea that the Garou's Rage utterly fucked up their entire purpose has been there since 1st Edition with the Imperium, War of Rage, and the idea behind Evan Heals the Past that wouldn't be a character we never talked about if they'd just done the senisble thing and made the kid a Child of Gaia and not a white boy who attended his first college courses. </div> </div> </div>[quote]<br /> <br /> Their Rage did not, in fact, do that. Their obsession with being on top did, via the ties that future Silver Fangs took to royalty, or their insistence on running the Impergium without the Ratkin. Those were done as close to stone cold sober as Garou get. Duty to the hero-kings got the rest to follow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I admit, it took the Sabbat and Second Inquisition books to finally turn me off V5. </div> </div> </div>Then now might be a good time to mention how future books seem to be pushing some &quot;brainwash into Hauglosk&quot; deal for the CoF that's right out of Danganronpa 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like my issues with this Edition can be summarized by pointing out that if they wanted to remove the Tribes from their cultural origins then maybe one of them shouldn't be named after a giant wolf of Norse mythology. </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. That's the most baffling part of the whole retcon business; why keep them around if they were the problem?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Make THEM the Winter's Teeth. </div> </div> </div>No. That's taken.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T13:45:46-08:00","id":1527195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527186#post1527186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Punk is not a title to be earned but simply an ethos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does he espouse objectively punk ethos beliefs, or even identify as one publicly? Even if you want to quibble about &quot;title&quot; punk is still label. Labels are useless if there isn't some level of definition for what does and doesn't belong within that label.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The final results are the Get of Fernis not being racially motivated so there's definitely that. </div> </div> </div>Sure, the problem is that just shifting it over to being fascists more broadly just means what sort of racial bigotry they hold is up for table-level decision making. Fascists always deal in racism or similar demographic bigotry, because they need out-groups to scapegoat.<br /> <br /> Nobody said anything about it being bad to have Nazi-punching in games. People said that how W5 handles it is bad, and you've said people have been depicting it unfairly (specifically that you believe the text is more nuanced than many other people are giving credit).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The take on the Cult of Fenris in the book is that they're a bunch of super-Garou theological fanatics that are trying to go after the Wyrm with reckless abandon. That's not, &quot;We believe only white people should be Cult of Fenris and all Garou should be Cult of Fenris.&quot; They're basically just following the typical Garou theology to its fundamentalist reactionary conclusion. </div> </div> </div>I asked for a citation of where the book demonstrates the nuance you said people aren't acknowledging. This is a passage that highlights how little nuance the Cult of Fenris really has.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note that you only get Hauglosk points when you violate a Chronicle tenet so literally you have to be a bastard against what the Chronicle is about to get any (unless you use it like the Dark Side of the Force for extra Willpower points). </div> </div> </div>That's for PCs. WoD5e doesn't like having rules for NPCs that apply consistently to PC rules. Like Sabbat on Paths, Cult of Fenris members are just different and NPC only anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The specific manifestations of hauglosk can take<br /> many forms. It\u2019s common for those who are afflicted to<br /> justify ever greater human casualties, ignore their own<br /> mistakes, and argue that everyone with even the mildest<br /> and most subjective whiff of corruption deserves to die.<br /> (In fact, such absolute terms are indicators, themselves<br /> \u2014 \u201ccorruption\u201d of that which is pure, \u201cdegenerate\u201d<br /> behavior or conditions, \u201csympathy\u201d for those who don\u2019t<br /> deserve it\u2026.) They often declare Garou who don\u2019t agree<br /> with them to be blood enemies, subject to even greater<br /> hatred than what a rampant Apocalypse has wrought<br /> upon the world.</i> </div> </div> </div>Right. As you can see with your own choice citations, the position of the Cult of Fenris is identical to how Hauglosk manifests.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if members of the Cult of Fenris all have Hauglosk 5 or not. Acting like you have fallen completely into Hauglosk is what being a member of the group is all about. It's a distinction without a difference. It's not nuance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T13:53:03-08:00","id":1527196,"title":"","content":"There is a section in the W5 corebook called &quot;Fascism&quot; which talks about the Cult of Fenris, Nazis, ecofascism, Hauglosk and how dealing with those things is an element in W5. And furthermore, thanks to James F. Sambrano's testimony we have &quot;behind-the-scenes&quot; context for that.<br /> <br /> You have to <i>ignore </i>the W5 corebook text to believe that Nazis, fascism, Hauglosk and the Cult of Fenris aren't <i>directly </i>linked to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T16:01:59-08:00","id":1527202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527196#post1527196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a section in the W5 corebook called &quot;Fascism&quot; which talks about the Cult of Fenris, Nazis, ecofascism, Hauglosk and how dealing with those things is an element in W5. And furthermore, thanks to James F. Sambrano's testimony we have &quot;behind-the-scenes&quot; context for that.<br /> <br /> You have to <i>ignore </i>the W5 corebook text to believe that Nazis, fascism, Hauglosk and the Cult of Fenris aren't <i>directly </i>linked to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Get of Fenris aren't Nazis save in the allegorical sense.<br /> <br /> Like the Galactic Empire or Daleks.<br /> <br /> They're absolutely racial supremacists but their race is Garou and their violent genocide is directed at humanity as a whole.<br /> <br /> This is important because it doesn't platform the real thing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T16:03:51-08:00","id":1527203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527195#post1527195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's for PCs. WoD5e doesn't like having rules for NPCs that apply consistently to PC rules. Like Sabbat on Paths, Cult of Fenris members are just different and NPC only anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, there's literally a loresheet in the back of the book about what to do when you're a Get of Fenris who wasn't corrupted by fanaticism.<br /> <br /> It's next to the loresheet that allows you to redeem Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> <br /> But yes, I think the nuance of the Cult of Fenris is the fact they're still fighting the Good FightTM. The book comments on the fact the Cult is engaged in the same battles that many of the Garou are still engaged in. They're the bad guys, absolutely, but I see them in the same sense as the Technocracy versus Mage. They're awful-awful people but have decent ends.<br /> <br /> Which is part of the tragedy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-21-2023, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T16:43:48-08:00","id":1527204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527202#post1527202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the Get of Fenris aren't Nazis save in the allegorical sense.<br /> <br /> Like the Galactic Empire or Daleks.<br /> <br /> They're absolutely racial supremacists but their race is Garou and their violent genocide is directed at humanity as a whole.<br /> <br /> This is important because it doesn't platform the real thing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, good thing we have a section in the book that clarifies the allegory: &quot;In the simplest terms, you can use Nazis of whatever stripe seems most appropriate for your setting as enemies.&quot; You notice the &quot;in the simplest terms&quot; there... I wonder where the idea came from to assume that now Werewolf the Apocalypse is the game where you fight Nazis...? Hey, we can't stop the Apocalypse but at least we have W5 now to platform fascists and that's where one really has to listen to the section on &quot;Fascism&quot;... The fascists shouldn't just be &quot;simple enemies&quot; after all. Good thing, we got the nuance on the fascists while fighting climate-change is considered a waste of time by W5 now (the Apocalypse is already underway anyway)...<br /> <br /> The meme one would usually connect with WtA is &quot;Furry Captain Planet&quot; but all of a sudden the W5 corebook is <i>convinced </i>an obvious enemy for a W5 game would be... Nazis. But you're not just fighting the fascists. W5 has a plot-twist there because maybe... you should play one! That's what the section on fascism in the W5-corebook is literally saying, roleplaying fascism is the point of a PC dealing with Hauglosk. Of course, nobody has to do that but whenever the W5-corebook talks about Hauglosk and Garou-culture in general, fascism is the real target of that negative commentary.<br /> <br /> Nazism isn't mentioned randomly in that section on fascism in the book. It's what the book invokes and wants you to think of when you look at the Cult of Fenris. Nazism and the Cult of Fenris are still <i>directly </i>linked.<br /> <br /> It's also telling that the Patron-Spirit of the Cult of Fenris is... the Wolf. When it comes to Patron-Spirits, it's obvious which one would probably represent the &quot;were-<i>wolves</i>&quot; most, right? The book in general is so negative about Garou that it's hard to tell what even is the difference between the Cult of Fenris and the other Garou at times...? They all can suffer from Hauglosk after all and W5's real-world analogue for suffering from Hauglosk is being a fascist. And it's not like the book believes other Garou to be some sort of noble counter-point to the Cult of Fenris.<br /> <br /> Also, by the way, this idea of the Cult of Fenris being a multi-Tribal coalition which you mentioned before... I agree that that's a better idea. The corebook doesn't support that but it's absolutely something that's happening in the Deepest of Wounds adventure. Like I said, H5 is worse but I think both games will suffer from their lackluster worldbuilding as Renegade keeps releasing more supplements. A corebook needs to offer a solid foundation and while W5 has done better in that regard both W5 and H5 have performed poorly on that count. That disdain for lore/worldbuilding in general has not worked out as a development-approach for those two books.<br /> <br /> With fascism playing such a central role in W5 and the book saying that &quot;Nazis&quot; are appropriate elements within the game... I think the realm of allegory has been left behind here anyway. You don't need allegories when the book is clearly spelling it out for the reader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T16:48:27-08:00","id":1527205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527202#post1527202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the Get of Fenris aren't Nazis save in the allegorical sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you recognize that they're Nazis in an allegorical sense, than the rest doesn't really matter. They're Nazis, and they need to be handled with the care that comes along with tackling Nazism in a game where your characters risk becoming Nazis instead of them just existing as punching bags.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is important because it doesn't platform the real thing.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Not supporting something isn't the same thing as doing a good job in denouncing it.<br /> <br /> Fascism and Nazism aren't mental health disorders you get from doing nebulous &quot;stuff&quot; (in the form of Chronicle Tenets) until you've become consumed by it. They're ideologies. They are taught to people, they are old to people, they are appeals to humanity that play off of the worst inclinations of humanity. Allegorical Nazis that became fascists because they became consumed by a magical mind corruption are not a good allegory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527203#post1527203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, there's literally a loresheet in the back of the book about what to do when you're a Get of Fenris who wasn't corrupted by fanaticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>And.., just like playing a Sabbat member that switch sides to the Anarchs or Camarilla in V5, it's just &quot;fluff.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You didn't get corrupted,&quot; so you aren't in the Cult, means being the Cult mean's your corrupted.<br /> <br /> Also, it's probably not a good idea to restart the &quot;BSDs can be redeemed, but CoF can only be prevented&quot; issues as far as allegories go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T16:59:12-08:00","id":1527207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527204#post1527204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, good thing we have a section in the book that clarifies the allegory: &quot;In the simplest terms, you can use Nazis of whatever stripe seems most appropriate for your setting as enemies.&quot; You notice the &quot;in the simplest terms&quot; there... I wonder where the idea came from to assume that now Werewolf the Apocalypse is the game where you fight Nazis...? Hey, we can't stop the Apocalypse but at least we have W5 now to platform fascists and that's where one really has to listen to the section on &quot;Fascism&quot;... The fascists shouldn't just be &quot;simple enemies&quot; after all. Good thing, we got the nuance on the fascists while fighting climate-change is considered a waste of time by W5 now (the Apocalypse is already underway anyway)...<br /> <br /> The meme one would usually connect with WtA is &quot;Furry Captain Planet&quot; but all of a sudden the W5 corebook is <i>convinced </i>an obvious enemy for a W5 game would be... Nazis. But you're not just fighting the fascists. W5 has a plot-twist there because maybe... you should play one! That's what the section on fascism in the W5-corebook is literally saying, roleplaying fascism is the point of a PC dealing with Hauglosk. Of course, nobody has to do that but whenever the W5-corebook talks about Hauglosk and Garou-culture in general, fascism is the real target of that negative commentary.<br /> <br /> Nazism isn't mentioned randomly in that section on fascism in the book. It's what the book invokes and wants you to think of when you look at the Cult of Fenris. Nazism and the Cult of Fenris are still <i>directly </i>linked.<br /> <br /> It's also telling that the Patron-Spirit of the Cult of Fenris is... the Wolf. When it comes to Patron-Spirits, it's obvious which one would probably represent the &quot;were-<i>wolves</i>&quot; most, right? The book in general is so negative about Garou that it's hard to tell what even is the difference between the Cult of Fenris and the other Garou at times...? They all can suffer from Hauglosk after all and W5's real-world analogue for suffering from Hauglosk is being a fascist. And it's not like the book believes other Garou to be some sort of noble counter-point to the Cult of Fenris.<br /> <br /> Also, by the way, this idea of the Cult of Fenris being a multi-Tribal coalition which you mentioned before... I agree that that's a better idea. The corebook doesn't support that but it's absolutely something that's happening in the Deepest of Wounds adventure. Like I said, H5 is worse but I think both games will suffer from their lackluster worldbuilding as Renegade keeps releasing more supplements. A corebook needs to offer a solid foundation and while W5 has done better in that regard both W5 and H5 have performed poorly on that count. That disdain for lore/worldbuilding in general has not worked out as a development-approach for those two books.<br /> <br /> With fascism playing such a central role in W5 and the book saying that &quot;Nazis&quot; are appropriate elements within the game... I think the realm of allegory has been left behind here anyway. You don't need allegories when the book is clearly spelling it out for the reader.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what your point is because:<br /> <br /> 1. Yes, obviously werewolves should kill Nazis. Heart of the Forest has flashbacks to about some Get of Fenris partisans fighting them get corrupted by their Rage.<br /> <br /> 2. Right Wing politics and anti-environmentalism are inherently linked.<br /> <br /> 3. The game makes it abundantly clear that the Nazis are the enemy.<br /> <br /> 4. They're &quot;Nazis&quot; but not actual white supremacists because they're bad guys that have a layer of fantastic racism to avoid platforming RL beliefs. It's like the Friends of Humaity or Orchis from the X-men. It's important not to platform RL racism but absolutely fine to have fictional allegories.<br /> <br /> Is there a dispute on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T17:04:21-08:00","id":1527208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527207#post1527207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what your point is because:<br /> <br /> 1. Yes, obviously werewolves should kill Nazis. Heart of the Forest has flashbacks to about some Get of Fenris partisans fighting them get corrupted by their Rage.<br /> <br /> 2. Right Wing politics and anti-environmentalism are inherently linked.<br /> <br /> 3. The game makes it abundantly clear that the Nazis are the enemy.<br /> <br /> 4. They're &quot;Nazis&quot; but not actual white supremacists because they're bad guys that have a layer of fantastic racism to avoid platforming RL beliefs. It's like the Friends of Humaity or Orchis from the X-men. It's important not to platform RL racism but absolutely fine to have fictional allegories.<br /> <br /> Is there a dispute on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no dispute except you just making my argument for me: Karim Muammar's idea of &quot;Get of Fenris=Nazis&quot; is still very much alive in W5.<br /> <br /> In W5 Nazis, fascism, Hauglosk and the Cult Of Fenris are <i>directly </i>linked to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T17:14:11-08:00","id":1527209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527208#post1527208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, no dispute except you just making my argument for me: Karim Muammar's idea of &quot;Get of Fenris=Nazis&quot; is still very much alive in W5.<br /> <br /> In W5 Nazis, fascism, Hauglosk and the Cult Of Fenris are <i>directly </i>linked to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they're the bad guys.<br /> <br /> That part is inarguable.<br /> <br /> But they're not racists or actual Nazis, just fanatical zealots and evil doers like the Technocracy. You can call the Technocrats Nazis but you're also engaged in misrepresentation even though they're fascist authoritarians.<br /> <br /> My issue is platforming actual Nazi and white supremacist rhetoric, which is a real danger. Having 90% of the Get turn to evil and the rest join the other tribes is a dumb plot point but it's not something that I can get worked up over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T17:40:11-08:00","id":1527211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527209#post1527209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean they're the bad guys.<br /> <br /> That part is inarguable.<br /> <br /> But they're not racists or actual Nazis, just fanatical zealots and evil doers like the Technocracy. You can call the Technocrats Nazis but you're also engaged in misrepresentation even though they're fascist authoritarians.<br /> <br /> My issue is platforming actual Nazi and white supremacist rhetoric, which is a real danger. Having 90% of the Get turn to evil and the rest join the other tribes is a dumb plot point but it's not something that I can get worked up over.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're acting like I'm the one who wants to platform fascist roleplay but... it's right there on pg 322: &quot;A player may decide to explore themes of ecofascism in their own character by skirting close to hauglosk.&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's fucked up. Cult of Fenris is a made-up term - ecofascism isn't. And so isn't Nazism. That section on Fascism says: &quot;In the simplest terms, you can use Nazis of whatever stripe seems most appropriate for your setting as enemies.&quot; The book literally says to make Nazis your antagonists. And the only Garou-faction mentioned are the Cult of Fenris. I wish the book showed more care in invoking things like that but there's no doubt that the W5 corebook wants to put the limelight on fascism and Nazism with the Cult of Fenris being their main-representatives. Not climate-change, though, don't bother making that a topic in a game... It's one of those &quot;systemic antagonists&quot; that would violate the holy &quot;street-level-only&quot;-rule of WOD5E. But instead, you can deal with ecofascism in W5. Either because you oppose it - or want to roleplay it.<br /> <br /> I mean, even if you have someone do this in good faith and with a genuine interest in roleplay: You talk about it with the people at your table first. Especially because it's mentioned in the same section as Nazism! It shouldn't be mentioned this casually!<br /> <br /> And the section about the Cult of Fenris is very unhelpful in that regard. Specific worldbuilding would help a lot here but... well, the WOD-team hates that, so there you go but take that line: &quot;The tribe\u2019s outlook is one of nonfalsifiable orthodoxy \u2014 impurity is everywhere and everything is the Wyrm\u2019s fault, and to disagree with this perspective is proof of one\u2019s own collusion with the Wyrm.\u200b&quot; What does impurity mean in that context? What does a viking-themed group of werewolves that cares about purity talk about when &quot;impurities&quot; are mentioned...? I wonder what's getting invoked here...? Of course, this is another &quot;Who knows&quot;-bit where the writing is lacking because of this disdain for lore/worldbuilding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T17:52:31-08:00","id":1527212,"title":"","content":"I was planning on giving W5 a hard pass, but I had a friend purchase a copy for me for Christmas (&quot;I saw they had a new edition of Werewolf and I remember you used to love the game. Merry Christmas!&quot;) I didn't have the heart to tell him I was planning to skip it. So I've been reading through it and I feel like W5 works pretty well for what it is - the game is intended to be a street level, short duration campaign. Unlike Vampire or even Hunter, I feel that the W5 play experience is intended to be wrapped up within a half-dozen sessions or so. It's not intended for chronicles to last years, the way Legacy editions or other WW games did.<br /> <br /> When you look at the mechanics you have the Harano/Haglusk mechanic. This mechanic slowly builds up until a character turns into an NPC. That sort of system is anathema to any long-running game. It's not uncommon in games for PCs to turn into NPCs for a short period of time (maybe a scene or so) but permanently? That sucks. So avoiding building up points on those tracks is imperative if you're looking at still playing this character in a year or two. On the other hand, the mechanic comes with a system where you can fill up the slots to get a boost in power, and that only makes sense if the assumption is that the game won't go on for too long. Who cares if your character is going to turn into an NPC if the chronicle is likely going to be over before that happens.<br /> <br /> That also dovetails with the lore. A lot of the lore is left as a mystery box. Nobody really knows what's happened in the ancient past, or even the more recent past. That's shitty worldbuilding, but it's fine for the intended play experience. Are the Silent Striders cursed? Who cursed them? How did it happen? Well it doesn't matter, it's irrelevant. Your PCs are going to be part of a street level, short duration chronicle. They aren't going to be instigating or solving the Silent Strider curse. That's well outside of the intended play experience. Did the War of Rage happen? It doesn't really matter. Your players aren't going to be fixing that issue or reconciling the Werewolves and other shifters. Maybe, if an ST wants to run with that, your group of PCs could make friends with some other shifters, but it's not going to be doing anything past that heal the past between Werewolves and Shifters.<br /> <br /> Finally we get to the intended playloop, which is fairly small scale and repetitive. The game isn't really designed for players to pick up, and become hobo/crusaders travelling around fighting Pentex and trying to save the world (in fact the group that does do that is the bad guys). Your players are intended to hang out in one place, protecting their touchstones and dealing with local problems. Some issue rears its head, the PCs smash it, and rinse and repeat. There's only so many times you can do this before things start to feel a bit stale, which is about when you'd start thinking of ending the game, probably by having the PCs launch an assault against the big bad guy who's been pulling the strings.<br /> <br /> This idea of localized gameplay is something that's part of the VtM play experience, but the difference is that faction politics are a big part of VtM, whether you're playing Anarchs of Camarilla, the idea is that you'll be spending a fair amount of the game focused on the local politics of the place you live. Not so with in W5. The game doesn't feel like it's intended that PCs are part of a large sept with a couple of dozen other members for PCs to engage in politics with. Rather it feels like they're intended to largely be on their own, which limits the kind of options that STs might have in their toolbox. Again though, if the game isn't intended to last beyond a half-dozen or sessions, then it's not a huge problem.<br /> <br /> So overall, I think for what W5 intends to be - a fairly short duration game where players play as street level characters with a basic understanding of the world who smash stuff up when it causes problems in their territory, it's actually pretty good. In that regard, I don't really have any problem with it. On the other hand, if you try to run W5 the same way you would run earlier editions of Werewolf, you're quickly going to run into a bunch of walls, whether from mechanics or the setting. At the very least your players are going to be sweating the Harano/Haglusk mechanic because they'll likely be worried about having to hand their character sheet over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T17:55:52-08:00","id":1527213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527211#post1527211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're acting like I'm the one who wants to platform fascist roleplay but... it's right there on pg 322: &quot;A player may decide to explore themes of ecofascism in their own character by skirting close to hauglosk.&quot;.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't being tempted by evil a very common roleplaying story?<br /> <br /> And yes, they use Nazis as a reference but also make it clear they don't hold any Nazi beliefs. It's used as a synonym for bad guy. But no, I'm absolutely not saying you're platforming or anything other than thinking this is a terrible idea. Which it may well be. Certainly, I feel the &quot;punching Nazis is good&quot; is a message I agree with but one thrown around way too casually as you say.<br /> <br /> I just don't think the Get are being treated as anything other than radical murderous fanatics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does impurity mean in that context? What does a viking-themed group of werewolves that cares about purity talk about when &quot;impurities&quot; are mentioned...? I wonder what's getting invoked here...? Of course, this is another &quot;Who knows&quot;-bit where the writing is lacking because of this disdain for lore/worldbuilding. </div> </div> </div>I mean, the one thing we know it can't mean is racial purity since the rest of the book establishes there's Get everywhere in the world.<br /> <br /> Just like every other tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-21-2023, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T18:04:39-08:00","id":1527214,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think the biggest issue of the book is the failure to provide mechanics for recovering from Harano or Hauglosk. They're meant to be recoverable but they don't say how.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Coming back from harano isn\u2019t impossible. </b>Some<br /> Garou rekindle their will to fight and rejoin the war<br /> against the Apocalypse. It would be foolish to say they<br /> come back stronger, because sometimes the weight of<br /> harano tangibly burdens even those who recover. Still,<br /> wise Garou take a long view often lacking in the young<br /> and hotheaded: They are still creatures of Rage but that<br /> Rage can be tempered by compassion. Perhaps, even in<br /> a society of monsters, misery loves company.<br /> <br /> AND</i><br /> <br /> <i>Hauglosk is a state of extreme righteousness.<br /> A Garou in a state of hauglosk believes that the<br /> cause is all, that their way is the only way. If<br /> more harm than good is caused, well, that\u2019s a<br /> cost that must be paid. Note that hauglosk<br /> is a long-term, <b>often </b>permanent, state and<br /> is thus different from Rage or frenzy (though<br /> hauglosk may well result in a destructive rage\u200b</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T18:16:46-08:00","id":1527215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527213#post1527213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't being tempted by evil a very common roleplaying story?<br /> <br /> And yes, they use Nazis as a reference but also make it clear they don't hold any Nazi beliefs. It's used as a synonym for bad guy.<br /> <br /> But no, I'm absolutely not saying you're platforming or anything other than thinking this is a terrible idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a reference?! Come on! Nazism is quite the reference, wouldn't you say? You're downplaying the extremity of the reference here. There are only two ways to look at this: Either the writers didn't understand what invoking Nazism would mean or they're saying you should think of antagonists/Cult of Fenris as Nazi-like. Considering that we know that one of the main-developers wanted the Fenrir to be Nazis, I think it's pretty clear how one can look at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527213#post1527213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the one thing we know it can't mean is racial purity since the rest of the book establishes there's Get everywhere in the world.<br /> <br /> Just like every other tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! I wish the W5 corebook had gone with something like that - but according to the book, it isn't that simple. From pg. 42: &quot;Only one thing is certain: Many Garou have Garou in their family lineages, whether human or wolf.&quot; But yeah, I know, just a page ago on pg. 41: &quot;No one knows. Everyone has an idea. As with so much else among the Garou, contention becomes conflict, and conflict risks violence. Since before recorded history, much debate has occurred, with some arguing heredity, some arguing spiritual intercession, and some trusting in a gnostic process that werewolves themselves simply cannot understand.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> And how about the Silver Fangs, the custodians of &quot;Pure Breed is actually good&quot;...? From pg 81 &quot;Werewolves of other tribes, particularly the young members of those of tribes, disavow \u201chereditary aristocracy,\u201d in which light the Silver Fangs cast themselves. Among tribal elders, anachronistic practices still hold sway, from Gaia-aligned notions of divine right, to the keeping of concubines, to simple affectations for outdated modes of dress.\u200b&quot; Aside from making it sound more like a bunch of vampire-elders... well, it's a mess. It probably would've worked better if the writers had actually done some more &quot;re-imagining&quot; here.<br /> <br /> But this also makes it clear where the Nazism-bit comes from: There's a strain in there that is still all about &quot;Get of Fenris=Nazis&quot;. The problem is that while there are attempts to cover up the idea, thanks to the &quot;lore/worldbuilding=bad&quot;-policy, there isn't a lot of room to hide the connection between Nazism and the Cult of Fenris in the W5 corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T18:22:51-08:00","id":1527216,"title":"","content":"As much as I'd enjoy a 'there but by the grace of Gaia I go' faction from the CoF, the way they are set up and how other tribes are set up prevents that.<br /> <br /> To begin with, Hauglosk is a one way street. You can shift your dots to Harano, but they can never be fully removed. Once you hit Hauglosk 5, your character is unplayable.<br /> <br /> CoF are stated to all be under Hauglosk and the tribe is defined by it.<br /> <br /> You can redeem a BSD, but the CoF loresheet implies the character just tipped their toe into the cult and even that nearly tainted them beyond redemption.<br /> <br /> Even though CoF are meant to be the ones taking things too far, the writing doesn't actually support it. Instead of 'they do what we do but take things too far', the message in the core is more along the lines of 'don't do what they do.' Which then creates the passive image of the playable garou.<br /> <br /> And in Deepest Wounds, the CoF are basically just written as BSDs, robbing the tribe of their own unique flavour.<br /> <br /> In addition, as much as Hauglosk and therefore CoF are stated to be examples of extremism, they are not.<br /> <br /> For one, BSDs aren't suffering from Hauglosk OR Harano. They do what they do with no mechanical mental health issues. If BSDs aren't used as examples of being maddened into extremism, then Hauglosk can't just be extremism.<br /> <br /> What makes this clearer is that Red Talon example characters include the following; A maneater, someone who intentionally infects towns with deadly diseases and someone who wants to put all of humanity into a cage and is doing so by being a bounty hunter.<br /> <br /> If neither BSDs nor Red Talons who kill whole towns are not suffering from Hauglosk, despite taking more extreme measures than the CoF in the core, then what makes the CoF bad is not being extreme.<br /> <br /> The only thing I can think of, is that they are a Nordic tribe and that is used as a shorthand for fascism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T19:23:20-08:00","id":1527220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527214#post1527214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think the biggest issue of the book is the failure to provide mechanics for recovering from Harano or Hauglosk. They're meant to be recoverable but they don't say how.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that's more a thing for NPCs, rather than for PCs. The mechanics are pretty solid in that those mechanics are one directional and once your character reaches maximum, they turn into an NPC. There's no recovering or coming back from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T20:13:16-08:00","id":1527221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527220#post1527220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like that's more a thing for NPCs, rather than for PCs. The mechanics are pretty solid in that those mechanics are one directional and once your character reaches maximum, they turn into an NPC. There's no recovering or coming back from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the maximum that worries me so much as everything before that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T06:11:52-08:00","id":1527232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527221#post1527221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the maximum that worries me so much as everything before that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to! Since there are no mechanics to high Harano or Hauglusk you will not be penalised or narratively changed in any way before your character is taken away from you. However, due to the way how touchstones work, you really are in a better position to endure Harano by taking as little Touchstones as possible, to limit how much Harano you can gain. Funnily, due to Hauglusk being tied into Tenets, it's quite possible to play a game about horrible, horrible people (like the out of the box Red Talons) and never, ever gain Hauglusk. And it's not like you need some demented BSD style tenets, just insisting on playing up the tribe ideals is enough.<br /> <br /> You gain Harano through failure and this is sped up with each Touchstone you lose.<br /> You gain Hauglusk through going against the Chronicle Tenets","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T06:21:23-08:00","id":1527234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527232#post1527232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No need to! Since there are no mechanics to high Harano or Hauglusk you will not be penalised or narratively changed in any way before your character is taken away from you. However, due to the way how touchstones work, you really are in a better position to endure Harano by taking as little Touchstones as possible, to limit how much Harano you can gain. Funnily, due to Hauglusk being tied into Tenets, it's quite possible to play a game about horrible, horrible people (like the out of the box Red Talons) and never, ever gain Hauglusk. And it's not like you need some demented BSD style tenets, just insisting on playing up the tribe ideals is enough.<br /> <br /> You gain Harano through failure and this is sped up with each Touchstone you lose.<br /> You gain Hauglusk through going against the Chronicle Tenets</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, I recently did a review of how to do Touchstones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/12/ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/12/ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/12/ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/12/ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T06:26:04-08:00","id":1527235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527234#post1527234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funnily enough, I recently did a review of how to do Touchstones.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/12/ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://unitedfederationofcharles.bl...nes-in-v5.html</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Good. You've clearly put into it more thought than they did in W5, where you get slightly over one page, with a heavy handed sidebar on how inappropriate it is to have Wolves for Touchstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T08:00:12-08:00","id":1527239,"title":"","content":"Honestly, for all the critique I have for W5, I do get the need for a much more down to earth game. I have heard many vampire players find it easy to get into, too.<br /> <br /> What bothers me is how clearly unfinished/unpolished parts are, how some are intentionally aggravated (see the CoF) and how there are things plain old missing.<br /> <br /> It is too easy and far too beneficial to lose the wolf if you don't want to deal with Rage. There are no rules for Gaia's Howl nor are there guides to making custom patrons. Wolf-born are included but extremely unwanted,etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T08:15:10-08:00","id":1527240,"title":"","content":"I thought I knew the problem, but apparently the hole is further down, so I'm going to ask, what's the problem with the Metis or born Crinos or whatever you want to call them? Yes, I know I missed the point, but I really don't know when I'll be able to ask that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T08:31:06-08:00","id":1527241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527240#post1527240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought I knew the problem, but apparently the hole is further down, so I'm going to ask, what's the problem with the Metis or born Crinos or whatever you want to call them? Yes, I know I missed the point, but I really don't know when I'll be able to ask that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is a terminology mixup with unfortunate implications. There are two similar words just spelled slightly different. One ties into a figure in greek mythology... The other into an offensive name used for mixed races of European and Native American extraction.<br /> <br /> Considering the breed is a product of a messed up union bringing forth a misbegotten child often referred to as a mule is the definition of unfortunate implications.<br /> <br /> White Wolf has claimed the intention never was to reference the people, but by the time they tried to disclaimer this it was already seen as deeply problematic.<br /> <br /> This is why people prefer crinosborn or warborn these days instead<br /> <br /> The other problem with metis is the fact that they are ostracized and mistreated by the rest of the Garou for the sins of thei parents and that they walk into the area that physical and mental disability are punishments from god.<br /> <br /> I do like them and feel there is a room for them, but they required a softer touch, and Paradox had none to give.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T08:54:12-08:00","id":1527242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527241#post1527241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Problem is a terminology mixup with unfortunate implications. There are two similar words just spelled slightly different. One ties into a figure in greek mythology... The other into an offensive name used for mixed races of European and Native American extraction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, one seems SIGNIFICANTLY more likely to be being what is referenced and it's not the Greek mythology one.<br /> <br /> Part of the issue seems to be the fact that a lot of the elements that the Garou nation had flaws: the fact they're racist, tribal (pun unintended), violent when unnecessary, and bigoted against their own members (see Crinosborn) are things that Alt-Right fans adopted for their own sake.<br /> <br /> TLDR: &quot;They didn't get the memo or didn't care these were the bad guys.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T09:04:05-08:00","id":1527244,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> there is a book reference that claims otherwise in Revised era. It was called out explicitly and a differentiation is made. Not that it matters at this point anymore, but let's not assume that old WW writers were assholes for asshole sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T11:18:45-08:00","id":1527254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527244#post1527244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> there is a book reference that claims otherwise in Revised era. It was called out explicitly and a differentiation is made. Not that it matters at this point anymore, but let's not assume that old WW writers were assholes for asshole sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always generally felt the majority of WoD writers were counter culture punks and progressive. It just happens when they screw up, it's very noticeable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T15:13:28-08:00","id":1527270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527241#post1527241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is a terminology mixup with unfortunate implications. There are two similar words just spelled slightly different. One ties into a figure in greek mythology... The other into an offensive name used for mixed races of European and Native American extraction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Small nitpick but worth pointing out: M\u00e9tis is not an offensive term when used in that context, but is a name for a specific ethnic group in Canada and the northern US that, as said, arose from the mixing of European and Indigenous cultures. Still <i>absolutely</i> not something you want to be connected to fantasy werewolves especially given what the Crinos-Born are, but it's important to note that it's not a slur.<br /> <br /> Count me in the camp that was disappointed that they were removed entirely instead of just renamed and reworked a bit, though. Even if it could be clumsy at times, it was still nice to see actual disability representation and the confrontation of issues around it baked into a game like this and it had loads of storytelling potential. Would have liked to see it truly polished so it could reach its full potential, but that would mean expecting W5 to put effort into literally anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T15:18:39-08:00","id":1527271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527270#post1527270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Small nitpick but worth pointing out: M\u00e9tis is not an offensive term when used in that context, but is a name for a specific ethnic group in Canada and the northern US that, as said, arose from the mixing of European and Indigenous cultures. Still <i>absolutely</i> not something you want to be connected to fantasy werewolves especially given what the Crinos-Born are, but it's important to note that it's not a slur.<br /> <br /> Count me in the camp that was disappointed that they were removed entirely instead of just renamed and reworked a bit, though. Even if it could be clumsy at times, it was still nice to see actual disability representation and the confrontation of issues around it baked into a game like this and it had loads of storytelling potential. Would have liked to see it truly polished so it could reach its full potential, but that would mean expecting W5 to put effort into literally anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue is not that they were disabled but they were supposedly &quot;cursed&quot; for being werewolf babies and were a hated in-universe group, which felt Ableist.<br /> <br /> Especially if you assume Gaia was the one who laid the curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T15:29:22-08:00","id":1527274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527271#post1527271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the issue is not that they were disabled but they were supposedly &quot;cursed&quot; for being werewolf babies and were a hated in-universe group, which felt Ableist.<br /> <br /> Especially if you assume Gaia was the one who laid the curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's part of the point, at least it is to me and a bunch of my other mostly-disabled troupe. While not everyone wants to, or should, have to deal with issues of marginalization within games if they don't want to, for some it can be empowering or cathartic to explore these issues within a fictional space or context. Disabled characters were there, explicitly, as a player option, and that's a lot more than most games give us.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;cursed&quot; aspect, I always felt that this was left up for interpretation in most versions, and is definitely one aspect that could stand to be clarified or reworked into something that wouldn't have these more problematic interpretations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T15:53:42-08:00","id":1527277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527271#post1527271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the issue is not that they were disabled but they were supposedly &quot;cursed&quot; for being werewolf babies and were a hated in-universe group, which felt Ableist.<br /> <br /> Especially if you assume Gaia was the one who laid the curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>They weren't really cursed, that is what some tribes thought, but garou born were no more tainted than any other garou by mechanics or lore.<br /> <br /> Their disability was the result of spiritual incest that garouxgarou pairings were. If there was any 'curse', it was that they were sterile, to make sure garou would not just breed with each other and become more insular than they already were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T16:09:30-08:00","id":1527278,"title":"","content":"While another old debate I'm not really feeling like revisiting in depth, a big problem with how things were handled (and &quot;spiritual incest&quot; isn't exactly different from a curse as far as things go) once the rest of the Fera were covered. There's little rhyme or reason to who's subject to &quot;spiritual incest,&quot; who's stigmatized, who's honored, who just can't make babies that way, etc. Since the spirits are metaphysically responsible for all of this, it just makes things messy in a bad way.<br /> <br /> I'm very sympathetic to the disability representation issue, but I think much like the indigenous representation that WtA was very unique for really putting up front as a major part of the game, the original version has aged incredibly poorly. There's so much better that could have been done than leaving things how they were, or just erasing it from the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T17:23:35-08:00","id":1527281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527278#post1527278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While another old debate I'm not really feeling like revisiting in depth, a big problem with how things were handled (and &quot;spiritual incest&quot; isn't exactly different from a curse as far as things go) once the rest of the Fera were covered. There's little rhyme or reason to who's subject to &quot;spiritual incest,&quot; who's stigmatized, who's honored, who just can't make babies that way, etc. Since the spirits are metaphysically responsible for all of this, it just makes things messy in a bad way.<br /> <br /> I'm very sympathetic to the disability representation issue, but I think much like the indigenous representation that WtA was very unique for really putting up front as a major part of the game, the original version has aged incredibly poorly. There's so much better that could have been done than leaving things how they were, or just erasing it from the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone should be ashamed for updating a setting either.<br /> <br /> White Wolf's position in the 90s was ham fisted, full of appropriation, and deeply wrong about some facts (the oppression of Native Americans isn't a &quot;both sides&quot; issue after all) but it was something that the company was taking a stance for and indigenous rights when it wasn't that long ago that Native Rights were a massively controversial issue at all. Hell, we're still building pipelines and installing things like blood quanta to limit their numbers.<br /> <br /> Updating it should be considered a good thing and not a source of shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T20:25:57-08:00","id":1527283,"title":"","content":"There shouldn't be shame for <b>trying</b> to updating the setting. Failing to accomplish your goals in said update is a different matter.<br /> <br /> The final version of W5 chooses erasure - a form of failure to the groups is poorly represented before - instead of providing them good representation. That's not really a fix to me. It's also hard to say that the setting was updated as opposed to just altered heavily. They want us to consider it a new game without continuity to the old, but they simply leave the setting unfinished with the lack of world building to replace what was cut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T21:51:50-08:00","id":1527284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527283#post1527283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There shouldn't be shame for <b>trying</b> to updating the setting. Failing to accomplish your goals in said update is a different matter.<br /> <br /> The final version of W5 chooses erasure - a form of failure to the groups is poorly represented before - instead of providing them good representation. That's not really a fix to me. It's also hard to say that the setting was updated as opposed to just altered heavily. They want us to consider it a new game without continuity to the old, but they simply leave the setting unfinished with the lack of world building to replace what was cut.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book has a page which details the role of indigenous cultures as well as their exploitation by Europeans so it wasn't a complete disaster, IMHO. I would have preferred more examples of the Native American septs that would make up the Gale Stalkers and Ghost Council. Basically, I would love for them to have cheated and went, &quot;Yes, the Gale Stalkers are a universal tribe but there was a HUGE chunk of them in the New World and they have their own political faction.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't have your cake and eat it to but you can certainly have two cakes.<br /> <br /> A Roanoke Gale Stalkers (or hell, maybe the Turtle children were a sept of Children of Gaia) sept that happened to have destroyed the Eater of Souls (acknowledging that the Croatoan are still around as a human people) is not erasing everything that came before.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T22:17:32-08:00","id":1527285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527284#post1527284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The book has a page which details the role of indigenous cultures as well as their exploitation by Europeans so it wasn't a complete disaster, IMHO. I would have preferred more examples of the Native American septs that would make up the Gale Stalkers and Ghost Council. Basically, I would love for them to have cheated and went, &quot;Yes, the Gale Stalkers are a universal tribe but there was a HUGE chunk of them in the New World and they have their own political faction.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't have your cake and eat it to but you can certainly have two cakes.<br /> <br /> A Roanoke Gale Stalkers (or hell, maybe the Turtle children were a sept of Children of Gaia) sept that happened to have destroyed the Eater of Souls (acknowledging that the Croatoan are still around as a human people) is not erasing everything that came before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that erasing Middle Brother would be a good move at this juncture, especially not with the CoGs. In some ways, it'd be like Evan Steals the Past, all over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T23:17:10-08:00","id":1527288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527285#post1527285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that erasing Middle Brother would be a good move at this juncture, especially not with the CoGs. In some ways, it'd be like Evan Steals the Past, all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they're already mentioned as a Sept that was destroyed, not a Tribe.<br /> <br /> <i>Modern Garou scholars hang their heads in shame as<br /> they recall such events as the slaughter of Garou and Kin<br /> in North America, and the subjugation of the Philippine<br /> Luntiang Kuko, a sept of witch-wolves that had protected<br /> the archipelago and significant portions of Southeast<br /> Asia. The White Howlers fell sway to the Wyrm and<br /> reforged themselves in its image as the Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> Over time, untold tribes and camps suffered \u2014 or<br /> chose \u2014 similar destruction, whether at the fangs and<br /> claws of other Garou, through choices to ally themselves<br /> with foul forces, or through abstention entirely from the<br /> once-sacrosanct compact with Gaia. <b>Some even disappeared,<br /> details unknown, such as the sept near the North<br /> American East Coast colony of Roanoke , which vanished<br /> without a trace.</b></i> Page 39<br /> <br /> But this is assuming that the Galestalkers and Ghost Council aren't Native American exclusively either. That there were always Twelve Tribes in the Pure Lands.<br /> <br /> Presumably like there's 12 Tribes in Norway during the Viking Era.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-23-2023, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T00:07:27-08:00","id":1527289,"title":"","content":"The whole thing of disconnecting Tribes from human culture comes off as half-assed without a lot of thought put into making it work, I think. Without the community feedback the Hart Wardens would still be the Fianna, for example. And the book never grapples with the idea of Tribes being everywhere and having no central hubs of presence in any region. And somehow the Silver Fangs are still big fans of hereditary aristocracy. The same effort of reworking the Native American Tribes needed to be applied to all the Tribes and it wasn't. (And even with the Ghost Council it's clear they just copied the name of JF Sambrano's version without coming up with a concept to justify the name)<br /> <br /> It's another bit of bad worldbuiling in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T01:21:04-08:00","id":1527292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527284#post1527284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book has a page which details the role of indigenous cultures as well as their exploitation by Europeans so it wasn't a complete disaster, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it is. The book never actually does anything with the impact f European colonialism besides use it as one of a litany of examples of how the Garou suck, but you're still supposed to want to play one for some reason.<br /> <br /> In the legacy editions (and even some fan attempts at fixing WtA's representational problems well before then) managed to make sure that the fight for indigenous rights mattered to the game. It wasn't a footnote of history (offensive since it is most certainly not just history) or and off-handed aside that's not even a story hook for anything.<br /> <br /> In W5, the Garou having participated in European colonial atrocities means nothing to the lives of modern Garou. They have no more reason to care than normal humans (and not particular means of doing anything about current indigenous rights issues besides dropping to Rage 0 and then engaging with things like a normal human would).<br /> <br /> Having more examples of indigenous peoples in the game doesn't make indigenous people feel like the game is empowering them as an important part of the humanity struggle through the allegory of the Garou. They don't need to be told that they exist, so Garou local to them are influenced by them, just like Garou everywhere else are influenced by the local population. It's just tokenism. It's saying, &quot;hey look, Native Americans, aren't we inclusive!&quot; without ever actually making indigenous experiences part of the game.<br /> <br /> And frankly, yes, focusing on the fucking Roanoke Colony story is erasure. It's a story about white colonists, not about the Croatoan people. The Croatoan didn't have one of their major settlements random disappear. That's not part of their heritage, or their stories. It's not about them, it's about British people. That means it absolutely should not be one of your centerpiece examples of Native American representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T02:24:19-08:00","id":1527293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527292#post1527292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure it is. The book never actually does anything with the impact f European colonialism besides use it as one of a litany of examples of how the Garou suck, but you're still supposed to want to play one for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you want to play Garou because you're a werewolf and that's awesome but the game rightfully questions any sort of self-agrandizing stories of righteous violence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In W5, the Garou having participated in European colonial atrocities means nothing to the lives of modern Garou. They have no more reason to care than normal humans (and not particular means of doing anything about current indigenous rights issues besides dropping to Rage 0 and then engaging with things like a normal human would). </div> </div> </div>I mean, they matter a great deal as examples of Wyrm and with the fact that Silver Fangs, Children of Gaia, Black Furies, and so on may well be indigenous peoples. Like I said, the fact that two of the four tribes of Native peoples are extinct in Werewolf Classic always rubbed me the wrong way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having more examples of indigenous peoples in the game doesn't make indigenous people feel like the game is empowering them as an important part of the humanity struggle through the allegory of the Garou. They don't need to be told that they exist, so Garou local to them are influenced by them, just like Garou everywhere else are influenced by the local population. It's just tokenism. It's saying, &quot;hey look, Native Americans, aren't we inclusive!&quot; without ever actually making indigenous experiences part of the game. </div> </div> </div>I mean the indigineous experience part of the game was wholesale cultural appropriation and selling it to the public. Not outright stealing terms, spirituality, and items is just as important as not misrepsenting their cause.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And frankly, yes, focusing on the fucking Roanoke Colony story is erasure. It's a story about white colonists, not about the Croatoan people. The Croatoan didn't have one of their major settlements random disappear. That's not part of their heritage, or their stories. It's not about them, it's about British people. That means it absolutely should not be one of your centerpiece examples of Native American representation. </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly. Removing its important place in Garou mythology as the massive extermination of a Garou tribal people is a pretty damn good thing. A single Sept of the Garou dying there keeps the story there without it becoming a massive white story about a Native sacrifice that never happened.<br /> <br /> I don't think the new version is great but I do appreciate that it was an attempt not to steal from other cultures anymore.<br /> <br /> And if you think I'm being too generous, absolutely the Patreon post by Sambrano pissed me off in how he was ignored and his ideas taken or brushed off. I think if they did want to wholly separate the tribes from ethnic lines, they still could have absolutely incorporated his ideas as groups within the tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-23-2023, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T04:05:34-08:00","id":1527296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527293#post1527293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you want to play Garou because you're a werewolf and that's awesome...</div> </div> </div> </div>What about being a werewolf in W5 is awesome?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, they matter a great deal as examples of Wyrm and with the fact that Silver Fangs, Children of Gaia, Black Furies, and so on may well be indigenous peoples. Like I said, the fact that two of the four tribes of Native peoples are extinct in Werewolf Classic always rubbed me the wrong way. </div> </div> </div>Except it isn't present as the deprivations of the Wyrm that the Garou were trying to stop, it's present as part of the endless stories of, &quot;every time the Garou try to do anything it's always horrible.&quot;<br /> <br /> It has no bearing on what's happening in the setting. It only matters if people at the table make it matter. There's no reason to explore other cultures when the game doesn't given you any cultures to explore (even fictional ones).<br /> <br /> I can make a Black Fury that has indigenous ancestry? I could do that already. The old books had the European Garou conquer the Americas and all that. Plenty of American born Garou are going to have some indigenous heritage from all the indigenous peoples that the Garou starting mating will. Not to mention that North America doesn't have some sort of ownership of indigenous people. There are indigenous people all over the globe. I could make characters from the Sami, or Ainu, or the Sorko people, and so on... and make it work with multiple Tribes from the old editions. Giving primacy to the impact of colonialism in the Americas without doing anything to center Native American issues isn't good.<br /> <br /> Just because it's different from the old editions doesn't mean it's actually better. It doesn't mean it's what the people that were appropriate from wanted out of W5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean the indigineous experience part of the game was wholesale cultural appropriation and selling it to the public. Not outright stealing terms, spirituality, and items is just as important as not misrepsenting their cause. </div> </div> </div>Right. Which is why they hired JF Sambrano to do it properly instead. Because that is an option. But Paradox balked at the work and effort, so they dumped that version for erasure instead.<br /> <br /> There is an option besides appropriation and erasure. Paradox had the chance to take it, and they didn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Removing its important place in Garou mythology as the massive extermination of a Garou tribal people is a pretty damn good thing. A single Sept of the Garou dying there keeps the story there without it becoming a massive white story about a Native sacrifice that never happened. </div> </div> </div>The story has no reason to be there at all. There are real stories that could be adapted instead. The fact that it's mentioned in W5 makes it far more important than it should be, because W5 is so stingy with its history and lore. Anything about the Roanoke colony should have just been cut. It's not a good story for WtA to bother with. It's not worth some minimized version either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think the new version is great but I do appreciate that it was an attempt not to steal from other cultures anymore. </div> </div> </div>W5 literally uses work by an indigenous TTRPG creative and author, and doesn't credit him. The couldn't even try to fix the game without stealing from a Native American. They had to redo artwork in the book because people noticed they appropriated Maori culture.<br /> <br /> No serious attempt was made if those things are true. Scrubbing off the worst of the outer layer isn't worth appreciation when they shoved more bad stuff under the rug.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you think I'm being too generous, absolutely the Patreon post by Sambrano pissed me off in how he was ignored and his ideas taken or brushed off. I think if they did want to wholly separate the tribes from ethnic lines, they still could have absolutely incorporated his ideas as groups within the tribes. </div> </div> </div>And yet, you're still being generous despite knowing all of that. You want them to get credit for treating indigenous culture issue better, despite the fact that they've objectively demonstrated they don't care about indigenous people at least at a corporate level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T06:10:07-08:00","id":1527297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527293#post1527293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you want to play Garou because you're a werewolf and that's awesome but the game rightfully questions any sort of self-agrandizing stories of righteous violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the game beats you over the head with the idea that you will never amount to anything because you can only ever be a destructive monster stuck between magically induced fascism and depression. The old game actually worked this out way better. It was clear that violence was not the ultimate answer and that you were dangerous to your surroundings, but it still made it worthwhile to be one and do something about the state of the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527293#post1527293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the indigineous experience part of the game was wholesale cultural appropriation and selling it to the public. Not outright stealing terms, spirituality, and items is just as important as not misrepsenting their cause.<br /> <br /> Yes, exactly. Removing its important place in Garou mythology as the massive extermination of a Garou tribal people is a pretty damn good thing. A single Sept of the Garou dying there keeps the story there without it becoming a massive white story about a Native sacrifice that never happened.<br /> <br /> I don't think the new version is great but I do appreciate that it was an attempt not to steal from other cultures anymore.<br /> <br /> And if you think I'm being too generous, absolutely the Patreon post by Sambrano pissed me off in how he was ignored and his ideas taken or brushed off. I think if they did want to wholly separate the tribes from ethnic lines, they still could have absolutely incorporated his ideas as groups within the tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div><img width=\"400\" height=\"400\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/xeIrQza.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/xeIrQza.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/xeIrQza.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Human culture is there to enrich us all and not everything is appropriation. There were some great talks about what is positive representation in old Werewolf, what is negative representation and which terms are problematic (with James, too). There's a lot of space to build upon here. I honestly cannot believe that you cannot see the difference between these two poles.<ul><li>having historic spaces where different cultures (especially marginalised ones today) have a chance to shine and take front stage without anyone else intruding upon that space and their own achievements within it</li> <li>having a minimalist nod to say &quot;your group could have been a part of this as well&quot; washing your hands of it and leaving the game as Europan/American coded as it is</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T08:52:01-08:00","id":1527301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527296#post1527296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, you're still being generous despite knowing all of that. You want them to get credit for treating indigenous culture issue better, despite the fact that they've objectively demonstrated they don't care about indigenous people at least at a corporate level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to rephrase then, &quot;I am not being generous and I'm disgusted with them for their behavior regarding Sambrano&quot; with the above being instead, &quot;I do think making Garou a more global phenomenon is the better idea.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is to say, &quot;Good idea, horrible handling.&quot;<br /> <br /> They should absolutely edit and credit him now as the bare minimum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The story has no reason to be there at all. There are real stories that could be adapted instead. The fact that it's mentioned in W5 makes it far more important than it should be, because W5 is so stingy with its history and lore. Anything about the Roanoke colony should have just been cut. It's not a good story for WtA to bother with. It's not worth some minimized version either. </div> </div> </div>The question is whether you want to remove wholesale large parts of the setting or not from the past or try to adapt them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can make a Black Fury that has indigenous ancestry? I could do that already. The old books had the European Garou conquer the Americas and all that. Plenty of American born Garou are going to have some indigenous heritage from all the indigenous peoples that the Garou starting mating will. Not to mention that North America doesn't have some sort of ownership of indigenous people. There are indigenous people all over the globe. I could make characters from the Sami, or Ainu, or the Sorko people, and so on... and make it work with multiple Tribes from the old editions. Giving primacy to the impact of colonialism in the Americas without doing anything to center Native American issues isn't good. </div> </div> </div>Actually, why I think it's a good idea is because America shouldn't be the focus of Werewolf at all. One of the things that 5E has done good on is the fact that it's properly acknowledging that every country in the world has WOD fans and can/should include their local people. One of the reasons I supported the removing of the Kuei Jin is because I've regularly communicated with fans and friends in Asian countries who HATE them.<br /> <br /> And a very good reason for that is, &quot;Because when I play Vampire in Hong Kong, I want to play a Tremere.&quot;<br /> <br /> You could argue that, &quot;Well you could always play a Tremere in Hong Kong, it just woudn't be a Kuei Jin&quot; but I feel that misses the point that the game is pressuring your experience. There's massive numbers of WOD fans in Europe, Mexico, Asia, and other places that can do local games that might benefit from the archetypes of Werewolf being present in their country from the very beginning.<br /> <br /> But you're absolutely right that removal is not a solution and I've mentioned multiple times I don't like the handling because they should have included the former positive representation as groups within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-23-2023, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T10:30:25-08:00","id":1527307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527301#post1527301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is whether you want to remove wholesale large parts of the setting or not from the past or try to adapt them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We already have the answer, and it's cutting W:tA down so that it's a side-hustle that doesn't threaten anything in V:tM. No expansive world of its own, no lore allowed, it's just VV5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, why I think it's a good idea is because America shouldn't be the focus of Werewolf at all. One of the things that 5E has done good on is the fact that it's properly acknowledging that every country in the world has WOD fans and can/should include their local people. One of the reasons I supported the removing of the Kuei Jin is because I've regularly communicated with fans and friends in Asian countries who HATE them. </div> </div> </div>Again, the writers had been on it since at least Revised, and wanted to do more. PDX just wants credit for other peoples' hard work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And a very good reason for that is, &quot;Because when I play Vampire in Hong Kong, I want to play a Tremere.&quot;<br /> <br /> You could argue that, &quot;Well you could always play a Tremere in Hong Kong, it just woudn't be a Kuei Jin&quot; but I feel that misses the point that the game is pressuring your experience. There's massive numbers of WOD fans in Europe, Mexico, Asia, and other places that can do local games that might benefit from the archetypes of Werewolf being present in their country from the very beginning. </div> </div> </div>This is a Vampire-specific issue, as its method of trying to incorporate undead like the jiangshi led to the &quot;only people of this ethnicity!&quot; supernatural ban on Hungry Dead coming from non-Asian people, whereas W:tA sports a society of living, flesh and blood (and spirit, but that's no impediment) that just need to have dates of being incorporated into a different region pushed back a few centuries (but they still ended up with non-European members far outside of Europe nonetheless). For a lot of locations, you can just say that they moved with the Silver Fangs, as the entirety of SF houses covers a very, <i>very</i> expansive area, and has a long history with where they are found.<br /> <br /> (A World of Rage has a nice tidbit about the Garou found among the Maori since there were Maori. They're Stargazers and Silent Striders, mostly. Later in the text implies CoGs were with them at some point.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you're absolutely right that removal is not a solution and I've mentioned multiple times I don't like the handling because they should have included the former positive representation as groups within. </div> </div> </div>I suppose I can only speak for myself, but it seems like if you have that feeling, it becomes really, really hard to like <i>anything</i> about W5. It's rotten from start to finish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T10:50:35-08:00","id":1527308,"title":"","content":"?<br /> <br /> V5 probably has the least non-US material of any of the editions based on the books released so far.<br /> <br /> W5 has........3-4 lines about the rest of the world. One of which is a single line about the Phillipines because a number of the writers were Pinoy.<br /> <br /> H5 has a section on the Phillipines because a number of the writers were Pinoy but the rest of the book is almost entirely US referencing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 12-23-2023, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T11:07:09-08:00","id":1527309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527301#post1527301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the things that 5E has done good on is the fact that it's properly acknowledging that every country in the world has WOD fans and can/should include their local people. One of the reasons I supported the removing of the Kuei Jin is because I've regularly communicated with fans and friends in Asian countries who HATE them.<br /> <br /> And a very good reason for that is, &quot;Because when I play Vampire in Hong Kong, I want to play a Tremere.&quot;<br /> <br /> You could argue that, &quot;Well you could always play a Tremere in Hong Kong, it just woudn't be a Kuei Jin&quot; but I feel that misses the point that the game is pressuring your experience. There's massive numbers of WOD fans in Europe, Mexico, Asia, and other places that can do local games that might benefit from the archetypes of Werewolf being present in their country from the very beginning.<br /> <br /> But you're absolutely right that removal is not a solution and I've mentioned multiple times I don't like the handling because they should have included the former positive representation as groups within.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those of us with friends and family in SE, South and East Asia that ST for and play Hungry Dead games far more often than they play the 'Hollywood Vamps' from VtM have different anecdotes.<br /> <br /> And dismiss it as much as you want but there are literally hundreds of references to Kindred being present throughout the world, they're like cockroachs they get everywhere and theres nothing at all, and a bunch of support for folks who want to play them there.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why you think there wasn't ample WtA material on Garou in Europe, Mexico, Asia, Africa, Australia, Antarctica, South America and numerous island groups because there really, really was.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T11:47:23-08:00","id":1527314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527308#post1527308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">?<br /> <br /> V5 probably has the least non-US material of any of the editions based on the books released so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>???<br /> <br /> The Camarilla, Anarch, and Sabbat books are massively international.<br /> <br /> Hell, its first and so far only major campaign released is the Fall of London.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T13:45:16-08:00","id":1527326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527301#post1527301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is to say, &quot;Good idea, horrible handling.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So... what is there to appreciate about W5's supposed better handling of indigenous issues? If the handling is horrible, than no matter how good the idea, the changes didn't actually make things better... and to many people made things around this specific topic worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The question is whether you want to remove wholesale large parts of the setting or not from the past or try to adapt them. </div> </div> </div>W5 did both when it felt like it. Anything to do with the Roanoke colony is firmly in the pile of &quot;should have just be removed wholesale from the setting,&quot; and they didn't even do that despite getting rid of Middle Brother anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, why I think it's a good idea is because America shouldn't be the focus of Werewolf at all. </div> </div> </div>That doesn't make any sense. I pointed out that the old editions had plenty of room for playing indigenous people from around the world. De-culturing the Tribes didn't actually make it suddenly easier to do so. W5 lacks both any serious focus on global indigenous issues so that people want to play games set in places other than their own home towns, any real discussion of what the new global Tribes really mean as global entities. <br /> <br /> The whole reason why representation is important, is because when you don't do good representation, minorities fade into the background and the majorities retain their status as the &quot;default&quot; in the setting. Tokenism, erasure, and so on aren't doing good representation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the things that 5E has done good on is the fact that it's properly acknowledging that every country in the world has WOD fans and can/should include their local people. </div> </div> </div>Your Vampire love is showing. The WoD was a global game before 5e, even if VtM sucked at it WtA certainly has lots of problems with how it handles non-European cultures, but the older Garou were already a global phenomenon that had a presence on six continents (Mage being Mage got to have mages in Antarctica too). WtA didn't have a KotE problem, because it had Asian werewolves well integrated into the setting well before that idea happened. Mage was global from the get go. Changeling and Wraith both established very early on that while the core book stuff wasn't global, they were global phenomena heavily influenced by local human beliefs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the reasons I supported the removing of the Kuei Jin is because I've regularly communicated with fans and friends in Asian countries who HATE them. </div> </div> </div>Well, there was a group of Asian fans that hated KotE... but instead of dumping the concept just did it the way it should have been done. That fan product is rather well regarded on the STV.<br /> <br /> Again, there are options besides dumping things. Not every Asian wants to play a Tremere in Hong Kong even if they also hated how KotE handled things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And a very good reason for that is, &quot;Because when I play Vampire in Hong Kong, I want to play a Tremere.&quot; </div> </div> </div>This feels... very weird as an example. WoD: Hong Kong established that Hong Kong is a stronghold of western Kindred, and the Tremere are one of the strongest Clans in the city. If you want to play a Tremere in Hong Kong, there was literally a book about that. Not just &quot;you could always do that,&quot; but it's an explicit part of the lore of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's massive numbers of WOD fans in Europe, Mexico, Asia, and other places that can do local games that might benefit from the archetypes of Werewolf being present in their country from the very beginning. </div> </div> </div>The thing about having so many Tribes in WtA, is that their archetypes aren't really that niche. You don't need the Silver Fangs in the Americas to play a member of Older Brother with strong family ties to the Aztec monarchy. The Silver Fangs never actually had an exclusive monopoly on such things, and their whole archetype only really matters once there's a Garou Nation for them to claim leadership of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T14:04:47-08:00","id":1527332,"title":"","content":"Eh, you have me <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> <br /> I'm not that enthusiastic about this and it's not a hill I particularly even want to defend let alone die on. I understand the desire to separate the culture of the Garou Nation from past appropriation but I don't support erasure, the handling of Sambrano' work, or particularly how they did the work as a whole which leaves me giving faint praise accompanied by huge heavy asterisks. You're absolutely right that they screwed it up and it is by far my least favorite part of the book that I would otherwise be very positive for. Just because I wasn't fond of how it was handled in previous editions doesn't mean I think the way they addressed it wasn't every bit as problematic in its own way.<br /> <br /> W5 has genuinely good points but they're wholly unrelated.<br /> <br /> Conceded.<br /> <br /> I do admit, though it's kind of funny that I'm known as the Vampire GuyTM who visits Weredom, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T14:06:01-08:00","id":1527333,"title":"","content":"On a related note, I'm going to start doing W5 essays like I did my V5 essays.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking:<br /> <br /> 1. Ten tips to handle the Cult of Fenris<br /> 2. 101+ Post-Apocalypse Werewolf adventure hooks<br /> 3. Ten Tips to handling Garou and their families<br /> <br /> At the start","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T23:58:18-08:00","id":1527347,"title":"","content":"Playing up the Post-Apocalypse nature of the setting sounds neat. Are you going to include how much the human world has been affected by the Apocalypse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T00:21:46-08:00","id":1527348,"title":"","content":"In fairness about the nationality thing, though; I have seen so many Nordic versions of <a href=\"https://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=Styrofoam%20Scot\" target=\"_blank\">Styrofoam Scot</a> in WtA games. Characters from the USA who know old norse/icelandic and apparently have kept to the traditions. Unless the PC is from Ymir's Sweat, those characters would know Swedish,Danish, Nowegian, Finnish OR Icelandic if their immigrant families were from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T01:35:32-08:00","id":1527351,"title":"","content":"There is, to a large extent, no helping that. Some people get really into an idealized version of another culture and... turn into that (with lots of different names around for which culture we're talking about).<br /> <br /> Media written by members of that culture can almost make people prone to this worse, because it just convinces them that they have an authoritative stamp of approval even if they're completely ignoring everything the creatives were trying to tell them. Just like there's never going to be a way for TTRPG creators to make rules that fully stop bad-faith players from doing disruptive things, they're never going to invite people to explore a culture without some bad apples making it about themselves instead of the people they're being taught about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T02:03:23-08:00","id":1527352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527351#post1527351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is, to a large extent, no helping that. Some people get really into an idealized version of another culture and... turn into that (with lots of different names around for which culture we're talking about).<br /> <br /> Media written by members of that culture can almost make people prone to this worse, because it just convinces them that they have an authoritative stamp of approval even if they're completely ignoring everything the creatives were trying to tell them. Just like there's never going to be a way for TTRPG creators to make rules that fully stop bad-faith players from doing disruptive things, they're never going to invite people to explore a culture without some bad apples making it about themselves instead of the people they're being taught about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I know, I mostly pointed this out because I finally found a word for it XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T02:05:57-08:00","id":1527353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527154-my-even-haded-review-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-fifth-edition?p=1527347#post1527347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing up the Post-Apocalypse nature of the setting sounds neat. Are you going to include how much the human world has been affected by the Apocalypse?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, it's hard to say what that would be because the Apocalypse is only noticeable from a spiritual perspective while presumably it's still recognizable our world in the homid one.<br /> <br /> I always wanted to do a Pentex Guide but there's some fantastic ones already. Sadly, I do feel the 21st century has illustrated accelerationist fundamentalist capitaliss are not in fact made up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T02:29:09-08:00","id":1527354,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the Apocalypse hasn't been redefined in W5. It's still the literal end of everything, both physically and spiritually. So the Apocalypse having already happened is completely impossible according to the book and being in the Age of Apocalypse should have a much more drastic effect on the setting.<br /> <br /> As for the Tribes... The only ones where you see any real effort to reimagen them are the Black Furies, the Galestalkers and the Ghost Council (which then indirectly also led to erasure as the representation wasn't then still highlighted somewhere else).<br /> <br /> With the rest, it was just erasure. Like the Silent Striders. Previously they were this nomadic Tribe connected to Egypt and the Followers of Set. The only change W5 made was to remove the Egypt bit and the connection to the Setites. Now they're instead cursed (?) by something (?). Removing these essential background elements should have called for some reimagening but W5 doesn't do that. It just removed the references and replaced them with question marks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","ti